#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Ticket work: a branch and worktree per ticket, the failure policy (retry, escalate, park), dispatch
of a headless or background session per ready ticket, a Claude cloud session on one ticket, the run records, the
budgets and the worktree list.

Usage:
    harness-work start N [--venue interactive|headless|bg|cloud]
    harness-work cloud N
    harness-work attempt N tests|breaker|code|review|fix|ci pass|fail [--tier sonnet|opus|fable]
                         [--effort low|medium|high|xhigh|max]
    harness-work stage N <stage> pass|fail [--tier T] [--effort E]
    harness-work cost N [--pr P] [--json | --markdown]
    harness-work dispatch [--max 10] [--venue headless|bg | --api] [--dry-run] [--only N[,N...] | --after N]
    harness-work dispatch --all-projects [--max 8] [--dry-run]
    harness-work dispatch --install-launchd | --uninstall-launchd
    harness-work runs [--sweep] [--all]
    harness-work waves [--all] [--refresh]
    harness-work wave drop ID N
    harness-work budget [status | exhaust api|cloud|subscription --reason TEXT [--hours 24]
                         | reset api|cloud|subscription]
    harness-work budget calls [--hours 24] [--json]
    harness-work worktrees [--stale DAYS]
    harness-work branches [--prune]
    harness-work worktree remove BRANCH [--discard]
    harness-work backup list [--all]
    harness-work backup restore ID [--path P] [--to DIR] [--force]
    start, attempt, stage, cost, dispatch, cloud, waves, wave, worktrees, branches, worktree and backup take --repo PATH
    (default: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, else the cwd's repository); every subcommand except worktree remove takes --json.

State, under ~/.claude/harness: repos/<repo-key>/tickets/<N>.json (the ticket cache that `harness-board show`
writes; start adds branch, worktree and started_at, attempt adds to attempts), repos/<repo-key>/cost/<N>.json (the
record `cost` writes), repos/<repo-key>/waves/<id>.json (a wave, harness_lib/waves.py), runs/<repo-key>-<N>-<stamp>.json
and .log (one dispatched run), budgets.json
({"api"|"cloud"|"subscription": {"exhausted_until", "reason"}}), backups/<id>/ (a snapshot, read by backup list and
restore), dispatch/launchd.log (the LaunchAgent's output).

attempt: appends {stage, tier, effort, result, at} to the ticket cache's attempts and prints the failure policy's
answer. The tier is --tier, else the stage's route (harness_lib.routing: review_route for review, code_route for the
other stages, from the cache's labels and the current settings), except that a coding stage keeps a cached sonnet or
opus (a cached fable is the pre-#239 rubric's and yields to the route; a cache without labels routes from its tier
as `harness-board tier` does, a cached fable reading as opus xhigh). The
effort is --effort, else the route's effort when the attempt ran at the route's tier, else none (null). The second
failure in a row escalates: sonnet prints `escalate opus`, opus with no effort or below xhigh `escalate opus xhigh`;
a stage already at opus xhigh or max, or on an explicitly named fable, gets park instead. No escalation goes to
fable. fix never escalates: retry, then park. A breaker failure answers done at any tier, however often (one
round; its gaps go to the coder as requirements). --json adds effort, next_tier and next_effort.

stage: records as attempt does (the same code, store and answer), then prints `next: <step>` on a second line
(--json: attempt's object plus "next"). retry and escalate repeat the stage; park names park; done
goes tests -> breaker (risk:high) or code, breaker (pass or fail) -> code, code -> review,
review and fix -> fix while the latest review round (harness_lib.reviews) has blocking findings, else ci,
ci -> `ultra, then ready` (risk:high) or ready. Risk and flags come from the ticket cache (risk,
flags, labels). Refused, exit 1 and nothing recorded: tests or breaker on a no-tests ticket, breaker on one that is
not risk:high, review or fix with no review round, fix pass while the latest round has blocking findings and fix
fail while it has none.

cost: ticket N's tokens and model time per stage and model from the repository's transcripts (harness_lib/cost.py's
ticket_usage), its labels and rounds from the ticket cache (the attempts replayed with attempt's rule; null without
a cache). From gh: the PR (--pr, else the cache branch's, a merged one first), its test/source/other lines, the CI runs
of its head branch, the needs-input count, the start-to-ready and start-to-land times, and the labels the cache
lacks; a failed gh call leaves its part null with one stderr line. Prints the stage x model table, the total, Claude
Code's session total for N's own sessions, the rounds, the Lines, Elapsed, CI and Needs input lines, the shared
sessions whose orchestrator is not counted, the lower-bound note and the saved path; --json prints the record,
--markdown the Cost block of the Resolution. Tokens and time only, no dollar figure.

start: refuses an epic, a closed issue, status:blocked, status:proposed and open blockers; fetches origin;
reuses a worktree already on t/N-*, else a branch origin/t/N-*, else a local t/N-*, else creates t/N-<slug> from
origin/main (main without an origin) in <main>/.claude/worktrees/t-N-<slug>; a new worktree gets HARNESS_WORKTREE_SETUP
(environment, then the project's .claude/settings.local.json, then .claude/settings.json) or the detected
setup (uv sync, npm ci); gitignored files of the main checkout matching .worktreeinclude are copied when
missing; a clean worktree, or a reused local branch, behind origin/<branch> is fast-forwarded to it, while a diverged
branch or a dirty worktree behind it gets one warning and is left alone; the ticket goes to status:in-progress,
except from status:in-review (a revision pass keeps its label) and from status:needs-input while the owner has not answered. For a needs-input ticket, `harness-board answers N`
runs first, before anything refreshes the ticket cache. --json prints previous_status (the status before start),
answers (the owner's replies; [] unless the ticket was needs-input) and waiting (needs-input with no answer).
An ops ticket (type ops, #72: a record update with no code change) gets no fetch, branch or worktree: branch and
worktree are null, the status moves as above, and --json adds ops (true) and before_dir,
~/.claude/harness/ops/<repo-key>/<N>/ (created), where the run saves the before-values before any write. A non-ops
start prints no ops key.

dispatch: sweeps the runs, then starts and launches each ready ticket (and each in-progress ticket whose last
run ended without a ready pull request, a draft counting as none, until 3 runs of it ended in the last 7 days,
a billing or auth run not counting) that has no live run, up to --max minus the live runs. --only N[,N...] plans just
the named tickets through the same path; a named ticket that is not such a ticket, or has a live run, is skipped
with its reason (printed, and in "skipped"). When the branch has an
open draft PR, the prompt and the start comment name it and say the worktree may hold uncommitted work from the
previous run. Launched sessions get neither
the dispatching session's identity nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN or CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN; when the
session is another project's (harness_lib.settings.other_project), CLAUDE_VERIFY_CMD and HARNESS_TEST_CMD are this
repository's from its .claude settings, left out where they set none (#299). bg, the
default whatever the budgets say, runs on the subscription: `claude --bg -n "<repo> #N <title>" --permission-mode
auto "/harness:work N"`.
headless, only with --venue headless or its alias --api (--api with --venue bg is an error): `claude -p
"/harness:work N"` billed to the API key through {"apiKeyHelper": HARNESS_API_KEY_CMD} (the key itself never
reaches a command line or the environment). headless while the api budget is exhausted (judged after the sweep,
which can be what exhausts it) is refused, --dry-run too: nothing starts, the exit is non-zero and the message
names the time and `harness-work budget reset api`. bg while the subscription budget is exhausted (also judged after
the sweep) is held the same way, --only, --after and --dry-run too: one line naming the subscription budget and its
reset time, exit 1; headless is not held by it.
An ops ticket never runs headless (it needs this Mac's connectors and credentials): a headless dispatch skips it with
a reason naming ops (printed as `skip #N: ...`, and in "skipped"); bg launches it in the main checkout (no worktree).
--all-projects (#164): one sweep of every run and the subscription hold, then each project of the registry
(harness_lib/registry.py) in its order: one whose .claude/settings.json committed at origin/main sets
HARNESS_AUTODISPATCH to 1 (a string or a number; never the working tree, settings.local.json or this environment)
and that has no open issue labelled incident gets this dispatch in the bg venue; any other is one
`<name>: skipped, <why>` line. --max (default 8) counts every live run record of every project (registered or not,
opted in or not) plus what this call launched, so each tick only tops up to the cap. A project that cannot be read
(its folder gone, not a repository, gh or harness-board failing) is one `harness-work: <name>: <why>` line on stderr;
the rest still run and the exit is 1 at the end. --json prints one document {all_projects, venue, max, dry_run,
live, projects: [{name, path, status dispatched|skipped|failed, why, result}]}. Needs no repository in the cwd.
--api, --venue headless, --only, --after and --repo with it are argument errors.
--install-launchd writes ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.ryaneskuri.harness-dispatch.plist (dispatch --all-projects --max 8
at minute 0 of every hour, StartCalendarInterval so an hour missed asleep runs once on wake; PATH as harness-digest's;
log ~/.claude/harness/dispatch/launchd.log) and loads it (bootout, then bootstrap gui/<uid>, else load -w);
--uninstall-launchd boots it out and removes the file, exit 0 when neither is there. Neither dispatches anything;
launchctl is HARNESS_LAUNCHCTL when set.
Effort: dispatch reads the routing settings once per command through harness_lib.routing.load_routing (environment,
else the main checkout's .claude/settings.json) and launches each session, redispatched ones too, at its ticket's
code route effort: HARNESS_CODE_EFFORT when set, else xhigh for a size:L or risk:high ticket (unless HARNESS_CODE_TIER
replaces the labels), as `--effort <level>` (bg: before the prompt; headless: last), writing `effort` to the run
record. With no effort: no flag, no key. An invalid value is one `harness-work:` warning on stderr per command (a dry
run and an empty board too) and is ignored. The dispatcher's own CLAUDE_EFFORT is never inherited. --dry-run's first line names the
effort when set (`Dry run: venue bg, effort xhigh, ...`); every --json result has a top-level `effort` (null when unset).
Waves (#180): with HARNESS_WAVE_REVIEW set (load_routing's wave_tier), the tickets one dispatch launched that are in no
unreviewed wave become one new wave (waves.create_wave, at that tier and effort xhigh), printed as `wave <id>: #12, #13
(reviewed together once all are in review)`; a redispatched ticket keeps its unreviewed wave, so a dispatch that
launches only those makes none. Every launched run record gets `wave` (its id) and every --json result a top-level
`wave` (the new id, or null). --dry-run prints `would group #12, #13 into a wave` and its JSON has `"wave": {"id":
null, "tickets": [...]}` (null when nothing would be grouped); it writes no wave. Without the setting nothing changes:
no wave, no `wave` key.

waves: this repository's waves (those with a ticket not closed; --all every one) as ID, TICKETS, STATE (empty,
working, due, reviewing, reviewed) and DETAIL (`1 of 2 in review; waiting for #13 (in-progress)`, `due`, `reviewing
(run <id>)`, `reviewed <time>`), the statuses from the ticket caches with no gh call; --refresh asks `gh issue view N
--json state,labels` once per waiting ticket and uses its status (a failing call is one warning; the caches are not
written). --json prints each wave record plus state, done, waiting and detail.

wave drop ID N: moves ticket N from the wave's tickets to dropped (waves.drop_ticket), so a wave with a stuck ticket
can become due; refused, one line and exit 1, for an unknown wave, a ticket the wave does not list and a wave whose
review was launched.

runs --sweep: closes the records of runs that ended and classifies each (ok, error, billing, auth; a bg run by its
`claude agents` state, done being ok). An `ok` run, headless or bg, whose issue is OPEN and still status:in-progress
with no ready pull request of its branch in any state (none, or only drafts) ended early: outcome `early`, shown as
`ended early (draft PR #N)` naming the open draft, else `ended early (no PR)`, even when the run has an exit code.
A bg failed or stopped run is never early. When gh cannot tell, or the record names no repository, it stays `ok`
with a warning. One command asks gh once per ticket and branch.
Every unended bg run's session transcript (~/.claude/jobs/<bg_id>/state.json's linkScanPath, else
~/.claude/projects/*/<bg_id>*.jsonl) is read for a usage-limit refusal: its last main-thread assistant entry with
isApiErrorMessage and apiError usage_limit_reached, no later user entry with usageLimitNote "release". It marks the
subscription budget exhausted until rate_limit_info.resetsAt, else quotaLimits.resetsAt, else its timestamp plus 5 h,
when that is still ahead; the record keeps it as usage_limit, so one refusal marks the budget once.
A cloud run ends on the latest marker comment (first line `<!-- harness-cloud: done -->` or `<!-- harness-cloud:
blocked -->`) by the gh user after the run's start, at that comment's time: done is `ok` (never early), blocked is
`blocked` and asks the owner (`harness-board needs-input` with the comment's other lines); else, when its ticket is
closed or a pull request of its branch merged, `ok`; else, 24 h after its start, `unknown`. Its status label never
ends it. A failing gh call is one warning and leaves it open. An unended cloud run is live.

cloud: refuses, before anything starts, a needs-local or ops ticket (run it here with /harness:work N), an exhausted
cloud budget, an unended cloud run of the ticket, a needs-input ticket with no answer since its question, and what start
refuses; then starts the ticket (venue cloud), pushes its branch with upstream (a failed push launches nothing) and
runs `claude --cloud <prompt> --on-branch <branch>` in the worktree with its stdout on a pseudo-terminal (claude
starts a new cloud session only from a terminal), without the credentials above. The prompt is self-contained:
repository, ticket, branch, the verify command (CLAUDE_VERIFY_CMD, else HARNESS_TEST_CMD, through project_setting:
from another project's session only this repository's settings count), `gh api` REST for comments and the two
markers; the session loads no harness plugin, hooks or
tests-first gate. claude's output without ANSI escapes and carriage returns is the run's log; the session id comes
from its claude.ai/code URL. The run record gets venue cloud, cloud_id and url, and the URL is commented on the
ticket. A failed launch, or one without a session id, ends the record in error with claude's last line; billing
wording there marks the cloud budget exhausted for 24 h.

branches (#416): origin's ticket branches (t/N-<slug>, read from origin with `git ls-remote`, never from
refs/remotes/origin) that no worktree has checked out, each with its ticket, its issue's state, its newest PR (`gh pr
list --head <branch> --state all`) and a stale flag. Stale only when the issue is CLOSED, none of its PRs is OPEN, no
live run record (run_live, every venue) names the branch, and its tip is the head of one of its PRs (refs/pull/N/head
on origin) or, with no PR, the issue was closed as completed. A failed or unreadable gh answer keeps the branch and is
one of its reasons. --json: [{branch, ticket, tip, issue ({state, state_reason}, null when unread), pr ({number, state}
of the newest, or null), stale, reason}]. --prune deletes each stale branch with `gh api
repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/refs/heads/<branch> -X DELETE` in the main checkout, never with git push (the pre-push hook
and branch_guard go on refusing a raw delete), and prints one line per branch: `deleted origin/<branch>: <why>`,
`kept origin/<branch>: <reasons>` or `not deleted origin/<branch>: <gh's error>`; a failed DELETE lets the rest run and
exits 1. --prune --json adds deleted (and error) to each row.

worktree remove: after the worktree and the local branch, a ticket branch's origin branch goes too when the branches
judge calls it stale, its tip read from origin (`deleted origin/<branch>: <why>`); else one warning `kept
origin/<branch>: <reasons>`, a failed read of origin or gh included, and the local removal stands. Nothing when origin
has no such branch. A failed DELETE is one line, exit 1.

backup list: this repository's snapshots (harness_lib/backups.py: its project store, <git common dir>/harness-backups/,
and its own in ~/.claude/harness/backups/), newest first, as ID, AGE, ITEMS (paths and git refs), SIZE and COMMAND; --all adds every
snapshot in ~/.claude/harness/backups/, and outside a repository list acts as --all; --json prints the manifests;
none is `No backups.`. backup restore ID: every item back at its path (`restored <path>` each), or with --path only
those at or under P, or with --to under DIR at its path relative to the snapshot's repository (else to its own
working tree, else its basename). Every target is checked first: an unknown id, or a target that exists, is one line,
exit 1 and nothing written; --force first snapshots the existing targets (into the snapshot's project store when it
sat in one, else where its repository's snapshots go now) and prints that snapshot's id. --path and --to are taken from the cwd.
Its git refs (not with --path) never touch a working tree: a branch comes back at its sha, HEAD as the branch
harness-restore/<ID>, changes and stash entries into the stash list (`git stash store`, the line naming the
`git stash apply` to run); a branch that exists refuses the restore, --force or not. --json prints {id, restored,
replaced, saved, refs} at the end.

A harness-board call that succeeds passes its `harness-board: warning:` stderr lines through to stderr, in order,
except a routing problem dispatch already printed (those children load the same settings; REPORTED); its other
stderr stays hidden. Siblings (harness-board) are found on PATH, else next to this script. gh is HARNESS_GH when set, else `gh`;
claude is HARNESS_CLAUDE when set, else `claude`. Now is HARNESS_NOW (`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`, UTC) when set and not
empty, else the real clock; an unreadable value is one line, exit 1, before any subcommand runs.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import datetime as dt
import json
import fcntl
import glob
import os
import plistlib
import pty
import re
import select
import shlex
import shutil
import signal
import socket
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import termios
import time
from urllib.parse import quote

_LIB = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), os.pardir, "lib"))
if _LIB not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, _LIB)
try:
    from harness_lib.paths import adopt_old_state, canonical_path, path_key, repo_key, same_entry
    from harness_lib.repo import NotARepository, RepoError, repo_facts, worktree_entries
    from harness_lib.routing import EFFORTS, cached_code_route, code_route, load_routing, next_route, review_route
    from harness_lib.settings import DEFAULT_SOURCE_EXEMPT, DEFAULT_TEST_PATTERNS, patterns, setting, settings_env
    from harness_lib.settings import committed_env, other_project, project_setting, setting_from
    from harness_lib.registry import load_registry
    from harness_lib.cli import Parser, Problem, emit, issue_number, run_main, table
    from harness_lib import backups, cost, reviews, waves
    from harness_lib.text import age_text as ago_text
    from harness_lib.text import first_line, harness_home, last_line, one_line, parse_iso, parse_iso_seconds
    from harness_lib.text import read_json
    from harness_lib.text import write_json as _write_json
    from harness_lib import gh as ghlib
    from harness_lib import ghlimit
except Exception as exc:  # no state key can be guessed without the lib: one line, exit 1
    sys.exit(f"harness-work: cannot load harness_lib from {_LIB}: {' '.join(str(exc).split())}")

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
STAGES = ("tests", "breaker", "code", "review", "fix", "ci")
TIERS = ("sonnet", "opus", "fable")
DEFAULT_TIER = "opus"
VENUES = ("headless", "bg")
BUDGETS = ("api", "cloud", "subscription")
DISPATCH_MAX = 10             # dispatch --max: live runs of this repository
ALL_PROJECTS_MAX = 8          # dispatch --all-projects --max: live runs across every project (#164)
AUTODISPATCH = "HARNESS_AUTODISPATCH"   # "1" in a project's committed settings opts it into --all-projects
LAUNCHD_LABEL = "com.ryaneskuri.harness-dispatch"
DEFAULT_KEY_CMD = "security find-generic-password -s harness-anthropic -w"
EXCLUDE_LINE = ".claude/worktrees/"
SLUG_MAX = 30
LOG_TAIL = 60                 # lines of a run's log read by the sweep
TAIL_BYTES = 256 * 1024       # of a run's log, and of a bg session's transcript (the usage-limit check)
USAGE_LIMIT_ERROR = "usage_limit_reached"   # a transcript entry's apiError when the subscription refused (#164)
USAGE_LIMIT_HOURS = 5.0       # a refusal that names no reset time: its timestamp plus this
SAFE_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$")   # a bg_id that can name a file
RECENT = dt.timedelta(hours=24)
REDISPATCH_WINDOW = dt.timedelta(days=7)   # an ended run older than this is not picked up again
REDISPATCH_MAX = 3            # ended runs of a ticket within the window after which dispatch skips it
UNCOUNTED = ("billing", "auth")   # outcomes of runs that do not count toward REDISPATCH_MAX: the budget's fault
EXHAUST_HOURS = 24.0
CALLS_HOURS = 24.0            # budget calls: the default window
CALLS_TOP = 15                # budget calls: rows of the text COMMAND table
REASON_MAX = 200
DIRTY_SHOWN = 10
GIT_TIMEOUT = 120
TOOL_TIMEOUT = 300            # a harness-board call
SETUP_TIMEOUT = 1500          # uv sync, npm ci
START_WAIT = 60.0             # seconds dispatch waits after a launch for the session's "Started on" comment (#367)
LAUNCH_TIMEOUT = 120         # claude --bg returns once the session is handed to the supervisor
AGENTS_TIMEOUT = 30
STOP_TIMEOUT = 30             # claude stop <id> of a finished ticket's session
GH_TIMEOUT = 60
BILLING_WORDS = r"credit balance|insufficient.*credit|billing_error|payment required|\b402\b"
BILLING_RE = re.compile(BILLING_WORDS, re.I)
CLOUD_BILLING_RE = re.compile(BILLING_WORDS + r"|credits? (?:are |is )?(?:used up|exhausted)|out of credits", re.I)
CLOUD_DONE = "<!-- harness-cloud: done -->"
CLOUD_BLOCKED = "<!-- harness-cloud: blocked -->"
CLOUD_SILENCE = dt.timedelta(hours=24)    # a cloud run with no marker this long after its start ends `unknown`
CLOUD_TIMEOUT = 300           # claude --cloud returns once the session is created
CLOUD_WINSIZE = (50, 400)     # the pseudo-terminal's rows and columns: wide, so the session URL is never wrapped
CLOUD_URL_RE = re.compile(r"https://claude\.ai/code/([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)[^\s\x00-\x20\x7f]*")
# CSI and OSC sequences and two-byte escapes; then the control characters a terminal leaves besides \n and \t
ANSI_RE = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-?]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\x1b\][^\x07\x1b]*(?:\x07|\x1b\\)?|\x1b[@-Z\\-_]")
CONTROL_RE = re.compile(r"[\x00-\x08\x0b-\x1f\x7f]")
AUTH_RE = re.compile(r"invalid.*api.key|authentication_error|\b401\b", re.I)
# A log line that is an API error from claude itself: without a JSON result (a crash before one), only these lines
# are searched for billing and auth wording.
API_ERROR_RE = re.compile(r"API Error|\"type\"\s*:\s*\"error\"|authentication_error|invalid[ _-]?(?:x-)?api[ _-]?key|"
                          r"insufficient credits|credit balance|billing_error", re.I)
# claude -p --output-format json on an API failure (seen with 2.1.296): is_error true, terminal_reason "api_error",
# api_error_status (401 ...) and claude's own message as the whole `result`. Only then is `result` read, anchored.
AUTH_STATUSES = (401, 403)
BILLING_STATUSES = (402,)
BILLING_RESULT_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:Credit balance is too low|Your credit balance|insufficient credits|billing)",
                               re.I)
AUTH_RESULT_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:Invalid API key|Not logged in|authentication)", re.I)
# A credential that can never work, seen on 2026-10-13 under statuses that are no auth status (400 "This API key is
# not scoped to a workspace ... anthropic-workspace-id header", 401 "Your apiKeyHelper script is failing"): a 4xx
# naming the API key, the apiKeyHelper failing, or the workspace header. "key" or "workspace" alone decide nothing.
CREDENTIAL_RESULT_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*API Error: 4(?!29)\d\d .*\bAPI key\b|apiKeyHelper script is failing|"
                                  r"anthropic-workspace-id", re.I)
BG_ID_RE = re.compile(r"backgrounded\s+(?:·|-)\s+(\S+)")
# `claude agents --json` states of a session still running; any other non-empty state means it ended. Seen on
# 2026-10-13: `blocked` for a background session; interactive sessions carry no `state` (a `status` instead).
LIVE_STATES = ("running", "working", "blocked", "idle", "busy", "waiting", "starting")
ENDED_STATES = {"done": "ok", "failed": "error", "stopped": "stopped"}   # outcome; another ended state is kept as is
# A ticket whose turn is over: its issue CLOSED, or OPEN with one of these. The bg supervisor marks a finished session
# `blocked` when its summary of the final reply suggests a next step for the user (#123), so the ticket decides.
FINISHED_STATUSES = ("status:in-review", "status:needs-input", "status:blocked")   # blocked: parked (#387)
PID_SLACK = 120               # seconds: a process younger than its run record by more is a recycled pid
# The dispatching session's own identity, which a detached run must not inherit.
SESSION_ENV = ("CLAUDECODE", "CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR", "CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT", "CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION",
               "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID", "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED", "CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET",
               "CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN", "CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH", "CLAUDE_PID", "CLAUDE_EFFORT")
# Credentials a launched session must not inherit: headless bills through apiKeyHelper, bg through the login.
CREDENTIAL_ENV = ("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", "ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN", "CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN")
# A project's own commands: a session launched for another repository than the dispatching session's takes them from
# that repository's settings, never from the dispatching session's environment (#299).
PROJECT_ENV = ("CLAUDE_VERIFY_CMD", "HARNESS_TEST_CMD")


def warn(text):
    print(f"harness-work: {one_line(text)}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def now():
    """The tool's clock: HARNESS_NOW (a UTC stamp `%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`) when set and not empty, else the real clock
    (#356). An unreadable HARNESS_NOW is Problem; main checks it before any command runs."""
    pinned = os.environ.get("HARNESS_NOW", "")
    if not pinned:
        return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)
    try:
        return dt.datetime.strptime(pinned, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc)
    except ValueError:
        raise Problem(f"HARNESS_NOW must be a UTC stamp YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ, not {pinned!r}") from None


def iso(when):
    return when.astimezone(dt.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def age_text(seconds):
    seconds = max(0, int(seconds))
    if seconds >= 86400:
        return f"{seconds // 86400}d"
    if seconds >= 3600:
        return f"{seconds // 3600}h"
    return f"{seconds // 60}m"


def write_json(path, data):
    """The lib's atomic JSON writer; a file-system failure is Problem("cannot write <path>: <reason>")."""
    try:
        _write_json(path, data, prefix=".harness-work-")
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot write {path}: {err.strerror or err}") from None


def wants_json(args):
    """Whether --json was given: a subcommand without the flag has no attribute for it."""
    return bool(getattr(args, "json", False))


# --------------------------------------------------------------- processes
def run(cmd, cwd=None, input=None, env=None, timeout=GIT_TIMEOUT):
    """Run a command and capture its output; a missing program or a timeout becomes a Problem."""
    io = {"input": input} if input is not None else {"stdin": subprocess.DEVNULL}
    try:
        return subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8",
                              errors="surrogateescape", timeout=timeout, **io)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise Problem(f"{cmd[0]} not found") from None
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot run {cmd[0]}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise Problem(f"{' '.join(cmd[:3])} timed out after {timeout} s") from None


def git(path, *args, input=None, timeout=GIT_TIMEOUT):
    return run(["git", "-C", path] + list(args), input=input, timeout=timeout,
               env=dict(os.environ, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT="0"))


def git_ok(path, *args, input=None, timeout=GIT_TIMEOUT):
    done = git(path, *args, input=input, timeout=timeout)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Problem(f"git {' '.join(args[:2])} failed: {last_line(done.stderr) or f'exit {done.returncode}'}")
    return done.stdout


def sibling(name):
    """A sibling bin tool: on PATH, else next to this script."""
    found = shutil.which(name)
    if found:
        return found
    here = os.path.join(HERE, name)
    if os.path.isfile(here) and os.access(here, os.X_OK):
        return here
    raise Problem(f"{name} not found on PATH or in {HERE}")


def claude_exe():
    return os.environ.get("HARNESS_CLAUDE", "claude")


def child_env(repo=None):
    """The environment for a launched session: ours, without the dispatching session's identity and without
    credentials that would bill instead of the apiKeyHelper (headless) or the subscription login (bg). When `repo`
    is another project's than the session's (other_project), PROJECT_ENV comes from `repo`'s settings alone, a name
    they do not set left out."""
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in SESSION_ENV and k not in CREDENTIAL_ENV}
    if repo is not None and other_project(repo.main):
        file_env = settings_env(repo.main)
        for name in PROJECT_ENV:
            env.pop(name, None)
            value = setting_from(name, file_env)
            if value:
                env[name] = value
    return env


# --------------------------------------------------------------- the repository
class Repo:
    """The project: its toplevel, its main working tree and its state key."""

    def __init__(self, path):
        try:
            self.root, self.common_dir, self.main, self.key = repo_facts(path, git, last_line)
        except RepoError as exc:
            raise Problem(str(exc)) from None
        self.name = os.path.basename(self.main)
        self.worktrees_dir = os.path.join(self.main, ".claude", "worktrees")

    def ticket_path(self, number):
        return harness_home("repos", self.key, "tickets", f"{number}.json")

    def cost_path(self, number):
        return harness_home("repos", self.key, "cost", f"{number}.json")


def open_repo(path):
    return Repo(path or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR") or os.getcwd())


BOARD_WARNING = "harness-board: warning:"
REPORTED = set()    # routing problems this process already printed; board() drops the same warning from its children


def board(repo, *args):
    """harness-board in the project; its stdout, or a Problem with its error line. On success its
    `harness-board: warning:` stderr lines go to our stderr, in order, except one already in REPORTED; its other
    stderr stays hidden."""
    env = dict(os.environ, CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=repo.main)
    done = run([sibling("harness-board")] + [str(a) for a in args], cwd=repo.main, env=env, timeout=TOOL_TIMEOUT)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        why = last_line(done.stderr) or last_line(done.stdout) or f"exit {done.returncode}"
        if why.startswith("harness-board: "):
            why = why[len("harness-board: "):]
        raise Problem(f"harness-board {' '.join(str(a) for a in args[:2])}: {why}")
    for line in (done.stderr or "").splitlines():
        if line.startswith(BOARD_WARNING) and line[len(BOARD_WARNING):].strip() not in REPORTED:
            print(line, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    return done.stdout


def board_json(repo, *args):
    out = board(repo, *args)
    try:
        return json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        raise Problem(f"harness-board {' '.join(str(a) for a in args[:2])} printed no JSON") from None


# harness-work's own wording for a gh call (`call` is its first two arguments), as its generic run() words it
WORK_GH_TEXTS = {
    "not_found": "{exe} not found",
    "cannot_run": "cannot run {exe}: {why}",
    "timed_out": "{exe} {call} timed out after {timeout} s",
    "failed": "gh {call} failed: {why}",
    "not_json": "gh {call} printed something other than JSON",
}


def gh_json(repo, args):
    """gh's JSON output (None when it printed nothing), run in the main checkout; Problem with gh's last stderr line."""
    return ghlib.gh_json(args, repo.main, pick=last_line, empty_ok=True, errors="surrogateescape", timeout=GH_TIMEOUT,
                         describe=lambda a: " ".join(a[:2]), texts=WORK_GH_TEXTS)


def api_key_cmd():
    """HARNESS_API_KEY_CMD from the environment, else `env` in ~/.claude/settings.json, else the keychain."""
    data = read_json(os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude", "settings.json"))
    file_env = data.get("env") if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("env"), dict) else {}
    return setting("HARNESS_API_KEY_CMD", file_env) or DEFAULT_KEY_CMD


# --------------------------------------------------------------- tickets
def read_cache(repo, number):
    data = read_json(repo.ticket_path(number))
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def slugify(title):
    slug = re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", (title or "").lower()).strip("-")
    return slug[:SLUG_MAX].strip("-") or "work"


def refusal(record):
    """Why a ticket cannot be started, or None."""
    n = record.get("number")
    if record.get("type") == "epic":
        tasks = [f"#{t['number']}" for t in record.get("tasks") or []
                 if isinstance(t, dict) and t.get("state") != "CLOSED" and t.get("number")]
        return f"#{n} is an epic; start one of its tasks" + (f": {', '.join(tasks)}" if tasks else "")
    if record.get("status") == "closed":
        return f"#{n} is closed"
    if record.get("status") == "blocked":
        return f"#{n} is status:blocked; read its comments, then harness-board status {n} ready"
    if record.get("status") == "proposed":
        return f"#{n} is status:proposed; it waits for harness-board promote {n}"
    blockers = [f"#{b.get('number')}" for b in record.get("blocked_by") or []
                if isinstance(b, dict) and str(b.get("state", "")).upper() != "CLOSED"]
    if blockers:
        return f"#{n} is blocked by open {', '.join(blockers)}"
    return None


def branch_refs(repo, prefix):
    """Short names under a ref prefix (refs/heads/t/, refs/remotes/origin/t/), newest commit first."""
    out = git(repo.main, "for-each-ref", "--sort=-committerdate", "--format=%(refname)", prefix.rstrip("/"))
    names = []
    for ref in out.stdout.splitlines() if out.returncode == 0 else []:
        if ref.startswith(prefix):
            names.append(ref[len(prefix) - len("t/"):])
    return names


def ref_exists(repo, ref):
    return git(repo.main, "rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", ref + "^{commit}").returncode == 0


def fetch_origin(repo):
    if git(repo.main, "remote", "get-url", "origin").returncode != 0:
        warn("no origin remote; branching from the local main")
        return
    done = git(repo.main, "fetch", "origin")
    if done.returncode != 0:
        warn(f"git fetch origin failed ({last_line(done.stderr) or f'exit {done.returncode}'}); "
             "working from the local refs")


def ensure_exclude(repo):
    """`.claude/worktrees/` in the shared .git/info/exclude, so the main checkout never lists the worktrees."""
    path = os.path.join(repo.common_dir, "info", "exclude")
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            text = fh.read()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        text = ""
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot read {path}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    wanted = {EXCLUDE_LINE, EXCLUDE_LINE.rstrip("/"), "/" + EXCLUDE_LINE, "/" + EXCLUDE_LINE.rstrip("/")}
    if any(line.strip() in wanted for line in text.splitlines()):
        return
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        with open(path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(("" if not text or text.endswith("\n") else "\n") + EXCLUDE_LINE + "\n")
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot write {path}: {err.strerror or err}") from None


def make_worktree(repo, number, title):
    """(branch, worktree, created): an existing worktree on t/N-*, else a new one on the right branch."""
    pattern = re.compile(rf"^t/{number}-.")
    git(repo.main, "worktree", "prune")                    # entries whose folder is gone would block the add
    for entry in worktree_entries(repo.main, git_ok):
        if entry.branch and pattern.match(entry.branch) and os.path.isdir(entry.path):
            return entry.branch, os.path.realpath(entry.path), False
    remote = [b for b in branch_refs(repo, "refs/remotes/origin/t/") if pattern.match(b)]
    local = [b for b in branch_refs(repo, "refs/heads/t/") if pattern.match(b)]
    branch = (remote or local or [f"t/{number}-{slugify(title)}"])[0]
    path = os.path.join(repo.worktrees_dir, branch.replace("/", "-"))
    if os.path.exists(path) and (not os.path.isdir(path) or os.listdir(path)):
        raise Problem(f"{path} exists but is not a worktree on {branch}; move it away, then start again")
    if branch in local:
        cmd = ["worktree", "add", path, branch]
    elif branch in remote:
        cmd = ["worktree", "add", "--track", "-b", branch, path, f"origin/{branch}"]
    else:
        base = next((ref for ref in ("origin/main", "main") if ref_exists(repo, ref)), None)
        if base is None:
            raise Problem(f"neither origin/main nor main exists in {repo.main}; nothing to branch from")
        cmd = ["worktree", "add", "--no-track", "-b", branch, path, base]
    os.makedirs(repo.worktrees_dir, exist_ok=True)
    git_ok(repo.main, *cmd)
    return branch, os.path.realpath(path), True


def catch_up(branch, worktree):
    """Fast-forward a clean worktree on `branch` that is behind origin/<branch> (a cloud session pushed there); a
    diverged branch or a dirty worktree behind it gets one warning and is left alone."""
    upstream = f"origin/{branch}"
    counts = git(worktree, "rev-list", "--left-right", "--count", f"HEAD...refs/remotes/{upstream}")
    if counts.returncode != 0:                              # no such branch on origin: nothing to catch up with
        return
    ahead, behind = (int(x) for x in counts.stdout.split())
    if not behind:
        return
    if ahead:
        warn(f"{branch} has diverged from {upstream} ({ahead} ahead, {behind} behind); left alone, merge or rebase "
             f"it by hand")
        return
    status = git(worktree, "status", "--porcelain")
    if status.returncode != 0 or status.stdout.strip():
        warn(f"{branch} is {behind} behind {upstream} but {worktree} has uncommitted changes; left alone")
        return
    done = git(worktree, "merge", "--ff-only", "--quiet", upstream)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        warn(f"cannot fast-forward {branch} to {upstream}: {last_line(done.stderr) or f'exit {done.returncode}'}")


def run_setup(repo, worktree):
    """HARNESS_WORKTREE_SETUP or the detected setup, in a new worktree; a failure is a warning."""
    cmd = setting("HARNESS_WORKTREE_SETUP", settings_env(repo.main))
    if not cmd:
        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(worktree, "uv.lock")):
            cmd = "uv sync"
        elif os.path.isfile(os.path.join(worktree, "package-lock.json")):
            cmd = "npm ci"
    if not cmd:
        return
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, cwd=worktree, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace",
                              stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=SETUP_TIMEOUT)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        warn(f"worktree setup `{cmd}` timed out after {SETUP_TIMEOUT} s in {worktree}")
        return
    except OSError as err:
        warn(f"worktree setup `{cmd}` could not run: {err.strerror or err}")
        return
    if done.returncode != 0:
        why = last_line(done.stderr) or last_line(done.stdout) or f"exit {done.returncode}"
        warn(f"worktree setup `{cmd}` failed in {worktree}: {why}")


def copy_includes(repo, worktree):
    """Copy the main checkout's gitignored files that match .worktreeinclude, when the worktree lacks them."""
    include = os.path.join(repo.main, ".worktreeinclude")
    if not os.path.isfile(include):
        return []
    listed = git(repo.main, "ls-files", "-z", "--others", "--ignored", f"--exclude-from={include}")
    if listed.returncode != 0:
        warn(f"cannot list the files .worktreeinclude names: {last_line(listed.stderr)}")
        return []
    inside = os.path.relpath(repo.worktrees_dir, repo.main).replace(os.sep, "/") + "/"
    paths = [p for p in listed.stdout.split("\0") if p and not p.startswith(inside)]
    if not paths:
        return []
    ignored = git(repo.main, "check-ignore", "-z", "--stdin", input="\0".join(paths) + "\0")
    if ignored.returncode not in (0, 1):                  # 1: none of them is ignored
        warn(f"git check-ignore failed: {last_line(ignored.stderr)}")
        return []
    copied = []
    for rel in sorted({p for p in ignored.stdout.split("\0") if p}):
        src, dst = os.path.join(repo.main, rel), os.path.join(worktree, rel)
        if os.path.lexists(dst) or not (os.path.isfile(src) or os.path.islink(src)):
            continue
        try:
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
            shutil.copy2(src, dst, follow_symlinks=False)
            copied.append(rel)
        except OSError as err:
            warn(f"cannot copy {rel} into the worktree: {err.strerror or err}")
    return copied


def hostname():
    name = socket.gethostname() or "localhost"
    return name[:-len(".local")] if name.endswith(".local") else name


def issue_labels(repo, number):
    issue = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "view", str(number), "--json", "labels"])
    labels = issue.get("labels") if isinstance(issue, dict) else None
    return [lb.get("name") for lb in labels or [] if isinstance(lb, dict)]


def start_ticket(repo, number, venue, draft_pr=None, announce=False):
    """Everything `start` does except printing; the ticket record, the branch and the worktree.

    A needs-input ticket's answers are read before `show` refreshes the ticket cache. The status goes to
    in-progress except from in-review (a revision pass) and from needs-input without an answer (waiting).
    `draft_pr`: dispatch's redispatch of a run that left only that open draft PR; a start comment names it.
    `announce`: a session's own start (`harness-work start`) comments "Started on" on a ticket already in-progress too
    (dispatch moved it there before the launch), so dispatch can see the session came up."""
    answers = []
    if "status:needs-input" in issue_labels(repo, number):
        found = board_json(repo, "answers", number, "--json")
        answers = found if isinstance(found, list) else []
    record = board_json(repo, "show", number, "--json")
    if not isinstance(record, dict):
        raise Problem(f"harness-board show {number} printed no ticket")
    why = refusal(record)
    if why:
        raise Problem(why)
    if record.get("type") == "ops":
        return start_ops(repo, number, venue, record, answers, announce)
    fetch_origin(repo)
    ensure_exclude(repo)
    branch, worktree, created = make_worktree(repo, number, record.get("title"))
    catch_up(branch, worktree)
    if created:
        run_setup(repo, worktree)
    copy_includes(repo, worktree)
    cache = read_cache(repo, number) or dict(record)
    if cache.get("branch") != branch or not cache.get("started_at"):
        cache["started_at"] = iso(now())
    cache.update(branch=branch, worktree=worktree)
    write_json(repo.ticket_path(number), cache)
    previous = record.get("status")
    waiting = previous == "needs-input" and not answers
    if previous not in ("in-progress", "in-review") and not waiting:
        board(repo, "status", number, "in-progress", "--comment", f"Started on {branch} ({hostname()}, {venue})")
    elif announce and previous == "in-progress":
        board(repo, "comment", number, "--body", f"Started on {branch} ({hostname()}, {venue})")
    if draft_pr:
        board(repo, "comment", number, "--body", f"Started again on {branch} ({hostname()}, {venue}): draft PR "
                                                 f"#{draft_pr} is open and the worktree may hold uncommitted work "
                                                 f"from the previous run")
    tier = record.get("tier") if record.get("tier") in TIERS else DEFAULT_TIER
    return {"number": number, "branch": branch, "worktree": worktree, "tier": tier,
            "title": record.get("title") or "", "previous_status": previous, "answers": answers,
            "waiting": waiting, "draft_pr": draft_pr,
            "type": record.get("type"), "size": record.get("size"), "risk": record.get("risk")}


def ops_dir(repo, number):
    """Where an ops run saves the before-values of ticket `number`, outside every repository."""
    return harness_home("ops", repo.key, str(number))


def start_ops(repo, number, venue, record, answers, announce):
    """start_ticket for an ops ticket (a record update, no code): no branch and no worktree; the before-values
    folder is created and named; the status moves as start_ticket's does."""
    before_dir = ops_dir(repo, number)
    try:
        os.makedirs(before_dir, exist_ok=True)
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot create {before_dir}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    cache = read_cache(repo, number) or dict(record)
    if not cache.get("started_at"):
        cache["started_at"] = iso(now())
    cache.update(branch=None, worktree=None, before_dir=before_dir)
    write_json(repo.ticket_path(number), cache)
    previous = record.get("status")
    waiting = previous == "needs-input" and not answers
    where = f"Started on the main checkout, ops: no branch ({hostname()}, {venue})"
    if previous not in ("in-progress", "in-review") and not waiting:
        board(repo, "status", number, "in-progress", "--comment", where)
    elif announce and previous == "in-progress":
        board(repo, "comment", number, "--body", where)
    tier = record.get("tier") if record.get("tier") in TIERS else DEFAULT_TIER
    return {"number": number, "branch": None, "worktree": None, "tier": tier, "title": record.get("title") or "",
            "previous_status": previous, "answers": answers, "waiting": waiting, "draft_pr": None,
            "type": "ops", "size": record.get("size"), "risk": record.get("risk"), "before_dir": before_dir}


# --------------------------------------------------------------- budgets
def budgets_path():
    return harness_home("budgets.json")


def load_budgets():
    data = read_json(budgets_path())
    data = data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}
    for name in BUDGETS:
        if not isinstance(data.get(name), dict):
            data[name] = {"exhausted_until": None, "reason": ""}
    return data


def exhausted_until(entry, at=None):
    """The time a budget is exhausted until, when that is still ahead; else None."""
    until = parse_iso(entry.get("exhausted_until")) if isinstance(entry, dict) else None
    return until if until is not None and until > (at or now()) else None


def exhaust(budgets, name, reason, hours):
    budgets[name] = {"exhausted_until": iso(now() + dt.timedelta(hours=hours)), "reason": one_line(reason)}
    write_json(budgets_path(), budgets)


def budget_line(name, entry):
    until = exhausted_until(entry)
    if until is None:
        return f"{name}: available"
    reason = one_line(entry.get("reason") or "")
    return f"{name}: exhausted until {iso(until)}" + (f" ({reason})" if reason else "")


def subscription_hold():
    """A Problem while the subscription budget is exhausted (#164): bg dispatch starts and launches nothing until the
    reset, a dry run included."""
    entry = load_budgets()["subscription"]
    until = exhausted_until(entry)
    if until is not None:
        reason = one_line(entry.get("reason") or "")
        raise Problem(f"the subscription budget is exhausted until {iso(until)}" + (f" ({reason})" if reason else "")
                      + "; nothing started. bg dispatch waits for that time, or `harness-work budget reset "
                        "subscription` once the limit has reset")


# --------------------------------------------------------------- runs
def runs_dir():
    return harness_home("runs")


def load_runs():
    folder = runs_dir()
    try:
        names = sorted(n for n in os.listdir(folder) if n.endswith(".json") and not n.startswith("."))
    except OSError:
        return []
    records = []
    for name in names:
        data = read_json(os.path.join(folder, name))
        if isinstance(data, dict):
            data.setdefault("id", name[:-len(".json")])
            records.append(data)
    return records


def save_run(record):
    write_json(os.path.join(runs_dir(), f"{record['id']}.json"), record)


def elapsed_seconds(text):
    """Seconds from ps's etime ([[dd-]hh:]mm:ss), or None."""
    days, _, clock = text.strip().rpartition("-")
    try:
        parts = [int(p) for p in clock.split(":")]
        day_count = int(days) if days else 0
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if not 1 <= len(parts) <= 3:
        return None
    hours, minutes, seconds = [0] * (3 - len(parts)) + parts
    return day_count * 86400 + hours * 3600 + minutes * 60 + seconds


def pid_alive(pid, launched=None):
    """Whether `pid` is still the process dispatch launched at `launched`: running, not a zombie, and not a
    recycled pid (a process that started well after the launch). The command line cannot tell: claude
    rewrites its process title to `claude`."""
    if not isinstance(pid, int) or isinstance(pid, bool) or pid <= 0:
        return False
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    except (OSError, OverflowError):
        return False
    ps = shutil.which("ps") or "/bin/ps"
    try:
        done = subprocess.run([ps, "-o", "stat=,etime=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True,
                              errors="replace", stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return True                                     # cannot tell better than kill did
    fields = done.stdout.split()
    if done.returncode != 0 or not fields:
        return False
    if fields[0].startswith("Z"):
        return False
    elapsed = elapsed_seconds(fields[1]) if len(fields) > 1 else None
    if launched is None or elapsed is None:
        return True
    began = now() - dt.timedelta(seconds=elapsed)
    return began <= launched + dt.timedelta(seconds=PID_SLACK)


def claude_agents(include_done=False):
    """{id: entry} from `claude agents --json`, or None when it cannot be read."""
    cmd = [claude_exe(), "agents", "--json"] + (["--all"] if include_done else [])
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace", stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                              timeout=AGENTS_TIMEOUT, env=child_env())
        data = json.loads(done.stdout) if done.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        return None
    if isinstance(data, dict):
        data = next((v for v in data.values() if isinstance(v, list)), None)
    if not isinstance(data, list):
        return None
    return {str(a["id"]): a for a in data if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get("id") is not None}


class Agents:
    """`claude agents --json` read at most once per variant."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.cache = {}

    def get(self, include_done=False):
        if include_done not in self.cache:
            self.cache[include_done] = claude_agents(include_done)
        return self.cache[include_done]


def is_bg(record):
    return record.get("venue") == "bg" or bool(record.get("bg_id"))


def state_ended(state):
    """Whether a `claude agents` state means the session ended: any non-empty state that is not a live one."""
    return bool(state) and state not in LIVE_STATES


def is_cloud(record):
    return record.get("venue") == "cloud"


def run_live(record, agents):
    if record.get("ended_at"):
        return False
    if is_cloud(record):
        return True                                     # until the sweep reads its marker, it is running out there
    if is_bg(record):
        listing = agents.get()
        if listing is None:
            return True                                 # cannot tell: never start a second run beside it
        entry = listing.get(str(record.get("bg_id")))
        return bool(entry) and not state_ended(entry.get("state"))
    return pid_alive(record.get("pid"), parse_iso(record.get("started_at")))


def tail_lines(path):
    """The lines of the last TAIL_BYTES of a file ([] when it cannot be read); the first may be cut."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            fh.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            size = fh.tell()
            fh.seek(max(0, size - TAIL_BYTES))
            data = fh.read()
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return []
    return data.decode("utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines()


def log_tail(path):
    return tail_lines(path)[-LOG_TAIL:]


def session_transcript(bg_id):
    """The main transcript of bg session `bg_id` (docs/research/usage-limit.md): the `linkScanPath` of
    ~/.claude/jobs/<bg_id>/state.json when that file names one that exists, else the newest
    ~/.claude/projects/*/<bg_id>*.jsonl (a subagent's file sits deeper and never matches); None when there is none."""
    if not SAFE_ID_RE.match(bg_id):
        return None
    claude_dir = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude")
    job = read_json(os.path.join(claude_dir, "jobs", bg_id, "state.json"))
    link = job.get("linkScanPath") if isinstance(job, dict) else None
    if isinstance(link, str) and os.path.isfile(link):
        return link
    found = glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(os.path.join(claude_dir, "projects")), "*",
                                   glob.escape(bg_id) + "*.jsonl"))
    found = [path for path in found if os.path.isfile(path)]
    return max(found, key=os.path.getmtime) if found else None


def usage_limit_refusal(lines):
    """The usage-limit refusal a transcript ends on: its last main-thread assistant entry when that is an API error
    with apiError usage_limit_reached and no later user entry released it (usageLimitNote "release"); else None.
    The fields decide, never the words: the text changes between versions and is quoted elsewhere."""
    released = False
    for line in reversed(lines):
        try:
            entry = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if not isinstance(entry, dict):
            continue
        if entry.get("type") == "user" and entry.get("usageLimitNote") == "release":
            released = True
        elif entry.get("type") == "assistant" and not entry.get("isSidechain"):
            limited = entry.get("isApiErrorMessage") is True and entry.get("apiError") == USAGE_LIMIT_ERROR
            return entry if limited and not released else None
    return None


def epoch_time(value):
    """A datetime from Unix seconds (a number, never a bool), or None."""
    if not isinstance(value, (int, float)) or isinstance(value, bool) or value <= 0:
        return None
    try:
        return dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(value, dt.timezone.utc)
    except (OverflowError, OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def refusal_reset(entry):
    """When a refusal's limit resets: apiErrorParams.rate_limit_info.resetsAt, else quotaLimits.resetsAt (Unix
    seconds), else its timestamp plus USAGE_LIMIT_HOURS; None when it gives none of them. The reset text is not
    read."""
    params = entry.get("apiErrorParams") if isinstance(entry.get("apiErrorParams"), dict) else {}
    info = params.get("rate_limit_info") if isinstance(params.get("rate_limit_info"), dict) else {}
    quota = entry.get("quotaLimits") if isinstance(entry.get("quotaLimits"), dict) else {}
    for value in (info.get("resetsAt"), quota.get("resetsAt")):
        when = epoch_time(value)
        if when is not None:
            return when
    at = parse_iso(entry.get("timestamp"))
    return at + dt.timedelta(hours=USAGE_LIMIT_HOURS) if at is not None else None


def refusal_text(entry):
    message = entry.get("message") if isinstance(entry.get("message"), dict) else {}
    parts = message.get("content") if isinstance(message.get("content"), list) else []
    texts = [p.get("text") for p in parts if isinstance(p, dict) and isinstance(p.get("text"), str)]
    return one_line(" ".join(texts)) or USAGE_LIMIT_ERROR


def note_usage_limit(record):
    """Mark the subscription budget exhausted until the reset of the usage-limit refusal that the transcript of a bg
    record's session ends on, when that reset is still ahead and this refusal has not marked it before; an exhaustion
    already running later is kept. The record keeps the refusal as `usage_limit` {"at", "until"} (budgets.json's
    entry is overwritten by `budget reset`), so after a reset only a new refusal marks it again. True when the record
    changed."""
    path = session_transcript(str(record.get("bg_id") or ""))
    entry = usage_limit_refusal(tail_lines(path)) if path else None
    if entry is None:
        return False
    until = refusal_reset(entry)
    seen = entry.get("timestamp") or str(until)
    marked = record.get("usage_limit") if isinstance(record.get("usage_limit"), dict) else {}
    if until is None or until <= now() or marked.get("at") == seen:
        return False
    budgets = load_budgets()
    current = exhausted_until(budgets["subscription"])
    if current is None or current < until:
        reason = f"usage limit: {refusal_text(entry)} (#{record.get('ticket')}, session {record.get('bg_id')})"
        budgets["subscription"] = {"exhausted_until": iso(until), "reason": reason[:REASON_MAX]}
        write_json(budgets_path(), budgets)
        warn(f"#{record.get('ticket')}: session {record.get('bg_id')} hit the subscription usage limit; the "
             f"subscription budget is exhausted until {iso(until)}")
    record["usage_limit"] = {"at": seen, "until": iso(until)}
    return True


def last_result(lines):
    """The last JSON object printed in the log (claude -p --output-format json prints one), or None."""
    for line in reversed(lines):
        text = line.strip()
        if text.startswith("{"):
            try:
                data = json.loads(text)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if isinstance(data, dict):
                return data
    return None


def matched_line(lines, pattern):
    for line in reversed(lines):
        if pattern.search(line):
            text = one_line(line)
            if len(text) > REASON_MAX:                  # a long JSON line: the part around the match
                found = pattern.search(text)
                at = max(0, (found.start() if found else 0) - REASON_MAX // 2)
                text = text[at:at + REASON_MAX]
            return text
    return None


def classify(lines):
    """(outcome, reason) of a finished headless run from its log tail.

    With a JSON result: is_error not true is `ok` whatever its text says; an API failure (terminal_reason
    api_error or an api_error_status) is `auth` on 401 and 403, `billing` on 402, `error` on 429 and 5xx, else told
    by the result text (claude's own message there: its start, or a 4xx naming the API key, the apiKeyHelper failing
    or the workspace header for `auth`), else `error`; any other is_error is `error` and its result text (the
    model's own words) is never read. Without a JSON result, the API-error lines of the tail are searched for
    billing and auth wording. Only `billing` and `auth` come with a reason."""
    result = last_result(lines)
    if result is None:
        lines = [line for line in lines if API_ERROR_RE.search(line)]
        for outcome, pattern in (("billing", BILLING_RE), ("auth", AUTH_RE)):
            line = matched_line(lines, pattern)
            if line:
                return outcome, line
        return "error", None
    if result.get("is_error") is not True:
        return "ok", None
    status = result.get("api_error_status")
    if isinstance(status, str) and status.strip().isdigit():
        status = int(status)
    if isinstance(status, bool) or not isinstance(status, int):
        status = None
    if result.get("terminal_reason") != "api_error" and status is None:
        return "error", None
    text = one_line(result.get("result") if isinstance(result.get("result"), str) else "")
    reason = (f"API error {status}: {text}" if status is not None else f"API error: {text}")[:REASON_MAX]
    if status in AUTH_STATUSES:
        return "auth", reason
    if status in BILLING_STATUSES:
        return "billing", reason
    if status == 429 or (status is not None and 500 <= status <= 599):    # transient whatever the text says
        return "error", None
    if BILLING_RESULT_RE.match(text):
        return "billing", reason
    if AUTH_RESULT_RE.match(text) or CREDENTIAL_RESULT_RE.search(text):
        return "auth", reason
    return "error", None


def mtime_iso(path):
    try:
        return iso(dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(os.path.getmtime(path), dt.timezone.utc))
    except (OSError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return iso(now())


def sweep(records, agents, as_json=False, dry_run=False):
    """Close the records whose run has ended; a billing or auth failure marks the api budget. A listed bg session
    whose ticket is finished has ended whatever its state says: it is stopped and its record closed. Saves. Under
    `dry_run` (dispatch --dry-run, #335) such a session is not stopped and its record is closed in memory only, with
    a `would stop session <id> (#N <state>)` line, so the plan still counts its slot free. Every unended bg record's
    transcript is read for a usage-limit refusal, which marks the subscription budget (note_usage_limit): a limited
    session stays `blocked`, a live state."""
    repos, logins = {}, {}
    for record in records:
        if record.get("ended_at"):
            continue
        if is_cloud(record):
            sweep_cloud(record, repos, logins)
            continue
        finished = False                    # None: the ticket could not be read, warned once
        if is_bg(record):
            if note_usage_limit(record):
                save_run(record)
            listing = agents.get(include_done=True)
            if listing is None:
                continue
            entry = listing.get(str(record.get("bg_id")))
            state = entry.get("state") if entry else None
            if entry is not None and state != "stopped":
                finished = ticket_finished(record, repos)
            if entry is not None and not state_ended(state) and not finished:
                continue
            if finished and dry_run:
                n = record.get("ticket")
                print(f"would stop session {record.get('bg_id')} (#{n} "
                      f"{finished_as(ticket_issue(record_repo(record, repos), n))})",
                      file=sys.stderr if as_json else sys.stdout, flush=True)
            elif finished:
                stop_session(record, as_json)
            record["ended_at"] = iso(now())
            if finished and not state_ended(state):
                outcome = "ok"              # a live state of a finished turn: the ticket says it is over
            else:
                outcome = ENDED_STATES.get(state, str(state)) if entry is not None else "unknown"
            code = entry.get("exitCode", entry.get("exit")) if entry is not None else None
            if isinstance(code, int) and not isinstance(code, bool):
                record["exit"] = code               # only when the listing gives one; headless runs keep null
            reason = None
        else:
            if pid_alive(record.get("pid"), parse_iso(record.get("started_at"))):
                continue
            record["ended_at"] = mtime_iso(record.get("log"))
            outcome, reason = classify(log_tail(record.get("log")))
        # a bg `done` is judged like a headless `ok`; failed, stopped and the rest never become early, nor does a run
        # whose ticket is finished (never in progress) or could not be read (warned already)
        early = ended_early(record, repos) if outcome == "ok" and finished is False else None
        if early is not None:
            outcome = "early"
            if early.get("draft_pr"):
                record["draft_pr"] = early["draft_pr"]
        record["outcome"] = outcome
        if outcome in ("billing", "auth") and not is_bg(record):
            exhaust(load_budgets(), "api", f"{outcome}: {reason}", EXHAUST_HOURS)
        if not (dry_run and finished):
            save_run(record)


def gh_login(repo, logins):
    """The gh user's login, asked once per command (a failure too); Problem when gh cannot say."""
    if "login" not in logins:
        try:
            logins["login"] = ghlib.gh(["api", "user", "--jq", ".login"], repo.main, pick=last_line,
                                       timeout=GH_TIMEOUT, describe=lambda a: " ".join(a[:2]),
                                       texts=WORK_GH_TEXTS).strip() or Problem("gh api user printed no login")
        except Problem as err:
            logins["login"] = err
    if isinstance(logins["login"], Problem):
        raise logins["login"]
    return logins["login"]


def cloud_marker(issue, login, since):
    """(marker, time, the comment's other lines) of the newest comment by `login` at or after `since` whose first
    line is a cloud marker, or None."""
    found = None
    for item in issue.get("comments") or []:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            continue
        author = item.get("author") if isinstance(item.get("author"), dict) else {}
        when = parse_iso(item.get("createdAt"))
        first, _, rest = str(item.get("body") or "").strip().partition("\n")
        if author.get("login") != login or when is None or when < since or first.strip() not in (CLOUD_DONE,
                                                                                                 CLOUD_BLOCKED):
            continue
        if found is None or when >= found[1]:
            found = (first.strip(), when, rest.strip())
    return found


def branch_merged(repo, branch, since):
    """Whether a pull request of `branch` (in any state) merged at or after `since`; False when the run names no
    branch. Branch names are reused (a reverted ticket starts a new run on the same t/<n>-x), so one merged before
    the run started is an earlier run's, and one without a readable mergedAt does not count (#295)."""
    if not branch:
        return False
    prs = gh_json(repo, ["pr", "list", "--head", str(branch), "--state", "all", "--json", "number,state,mergedAt",
                         "--limit", str(PR_ROWS)])
    rows = prs if isinstance(prs, list) else []
    for pr in rows:
        if not isinstance(pr, dict) or str(pr.get("state", "")).upper() != "MERGED":
            continue
        when = parse_iso(pr.get("mergedAt"))
        if when is not None and when >= since:
            return True
    return False


def sweep_cloud(record, repos, logins):
    """Close a cloud run from its ticket: the newest marker comment by the gh user since the start (done: ok;
    blocked: blocked, the owner asked through harness-board needs-input), else a closed ticket or a pull request of
    its branch merged since the start (ok), else 24 h since the start (unknown). Its status label never ends it: a cloud session
    can still be working on a ticket left needs-input or ready (#295). A failing gh call is one warning and leaves
    the run open. Saves when it closes."""
    n = record.get("ticket")
    if not isinstance(n, int):
        return
    started = parse_iso(record.get("started_at")) or now()
    try:
        repo = record_repo(record, repos)
        issue = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "view", str(n), "--json", "number,title,state,labels,comments"])
        if not isinstance(issue, dict):
            raise Problem(f"gh issue view {n} printed no issue")
        marker = cloud_marker(issue, gh_login(repo, logins), started)
    except Problem as err:
        warn(f"#{n}: cannot read how its cloud run is doing: {err}")
        return
    if marker is not None:
        kind, when, rest = marker
        if kind == CLOUD_BLOCKED:
            question = rest or (f"The cloud session on {record.get('branch')} stopped blocked without a question; "
                                f"see {record.get('url')}")
            try:
                board(repo, "needs-input", n, "--question", question)
            except Problem as err:
                warn(f"#{n}: its cloud run is blocked, but the question could not be asked: {err}")
                return
        outcome, ended = ("blocked" if kind == CLOUD_BLOCKED else "ok"), iso(when)
    elif str(issue.get("state", "")).upper() == "CLOSED":
        outcome, ended = "ok", iso(now())
    else:
        try:
            merged = branch_merged(repo, record.get("branch"), started)
        except Problem as err:
            warn(f"#{n}: cannot tell whether a pull request of its cloud run merged: {err}")
            return
        if merged:
            outcome, ended = "ok", iso(now())
        elif now() - started >= CLOUD_SILENCE:
            outcome, ended = "unknown", iso(now())
        else:
            return
    record.update(ended_at=ended, outcome=outcome)
    save_run(record)


def ended_early(record, repos):
    """The issue (as without_pr gives it) when an `ok` run (headless, or bg `done`) left its ticket in progress with no
    ready pull request: the session ended its turn before the work did. None, with a warning, when the repository or
    gh cannot tell. `repos` caches Repo by path."""
    n = record.get("ticket")
    if not isinstance(n, int):
        return None
    try:
        return without_pr(record_repo(record, repos), n, record.get("branch"))
    except Problem as err:
        warn(f"#{n}: cannot check whether its run ended early: {err}")
        return None


def record_repo(record, repos):
    """The Repo a run record names, cached in `repos` by path; a Problem when it names none or it cannot be opened.
    Never the cwd's repository: its issue n may be another ticket."""
    path = str(record.get("repo") or "")
    if not path:
        raise Problem("the run record names no repository")
    if path not in repos:
        repos[path] = Repo(path)
    return repos[path]


def issue_finished(issue):
    """Whether a ticket's turn is over: its issue CLOSED (whatever labels it kept), or OPEN with status:in-review,
    status:needs-input or status:blocked (parked, #387). In progress, ready or without a status, it is not."""
    if not isinstance(issue, dict):
        return False
    state = str(issue.get("state", "")).upper()
    labels = [lb.get("name") for lb in issue.get("labels") or [] if isinstance(lb, dict)]
    return state == "CLOSED" or (state == "OPEN" and any(lb in FINISHED_STATUSES for lb in labels))


def finished_as(issue):
    """Why issue_finished says a ticket's turn is over: `closed`, or its finished status label."""
    if str(issue.get("state", "")).upper() == "CLOSED":
        return "closed"
    labels = [lb.get("name") for lb in issue.get("labels") or [] if isinstance(lb, dict)]
    return next((lb for lb in labels if lb in FINISHED_STATUSES), "finished")


def ticket_finished(record, repos):
    """Whether the ticket of a run is finished (issue_finished); None, with a warning, when the repository or gh
    cannot tell, so the session is neither stopped nor counted ended."""
    n = record.get("ticket")
    if not isinstance(n, int):
        return None
    try:
        return issue_finished(ticket_issue(record_repo(record, repos), n))
    except Problem as err:
        warn(f"#{n}: cannot tell whether its ticket is finished: {err}")
        return None


def stop_bg(record):
    """`claude stop <id>` for the bg session of a record: None when it stopped, else why it did not."""
    try:
        done = run([claude_exe(), "stop", str(record.get("bg_id"))], env=child_env(), timeout=STOP_TIMEOUT)
        return None if done.returncode == 0 else (last_line(done.stderr) or last_line(done.stdout)
                                                  or f"exit {done.returncode}")
    except Problem as err:
        return str(err)


def stop_session(record, as_json):
    """Stop the bg session of a finished ticket (its conversation is kept): `stopped session <id>` on stdout (stderr
    under --json, which keeps stdout whole), or one warning when it fails."""
    bg_id = str(record.get("bg_id"))
    why = stop_bg(record)
    if why is not None:
        warn(f"#{record.get('ticket')}: cannot stop session {bg_id}: {why}")
        return
    print(f"stopped session {bg_id}", file=sys.stderr if as_json else sys.stdout, flush=True)


def run_state(record, agents):
    if record.get("ended_at"):
        if record.get("outcome") == "early":           # wins over an exit code: the 0 of a done bg run says less
            pr = record.get("draft_pr")
            return f"ended early (draft PR #{pr})" if pr else "ended early (no PR)"
        exit_code = record.get("exit")
        if exit_code is not None:
            return f"exited {exit_code}"
        return f"ended {record.get('outcome') or '?'}"
    if is_cloud(record):
        return f"in the cloud ({record.get('url')})"
    if is_bg(record):
        listing = agents.get()
        entry = listing.get(str(record.get("bg_id"))) if listing else None
        if entry and not state_ended(entry.get("state")):
            return entry.get("state") or "live"
        return "unknown" if listing is None else "ended (run --sweep)"
    alive = pid_alive(record.get("pid"), parse_iso(record.get("started_at")))
    return f"alive (pid {record.get('pid')})" if alive else "exited (run --sweep)"


def of_repo(record, repo):
    """By the repo field in any spelling of the main tree (runs before the canonical key), else by the id."""
    field = record.get("repo")
    return (field == repo.main or (isinstance(field, str) and field != "" and canonical_path(field) == repo.main)
            or str(record.get("id", "")).startswith(repo.key + "-"))


# --------------------------------------------------------------- launching
def launch(repo, ticket, venue, effort=None):
    """Start one session for a started ticket and write its run record. `effort` (a level or None) goes to the
    session as --effort and into the record; unset, the session gets no --effort and the record no effort key."""
    n = ticket["number"]
    started = now()
    rid = f"{repo.key}-{n}-{started.strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M%S')}"
    log = os.path.join(runs_dir(), f"{rid}.log")
    os.makedirs(runs_dir(), exist_ok=True)
    record = {"id": rid, "ticket": n, "repo": repo.main, "worktree": ticket["worktree"], "branch": ticket["branch"],
              "venue": venue, "log": log, "started_at": iso(started), "ended_at": None, "exit": None,
              "outcome": None}
    if effort:
        record["effort"] = effort
    prompt = f"/harness:work {n}"
    cwd = ticket["worktree"] or repo.main      # an ops ticket has no worktree: its session runs in the main checkout
    if ticket.get("draft_pr"):
        prompt += (f"\n\nThe previous run ended early: draft PR #{ticket['draft_pr']} is open and the worktree may "
                   f"hold uncommitted work from that run. Read `git status` and the PR's review comments before "
                   f"deciding what to do.")
    if venue == "headless":
        settings = json.dumps({"apiKeyHelper": api_key_cmd()})
        argv = [claude_exe(), "-p", prompt, "--permission-mode", "auto", "--output-format", "json",
                "--settings", settings]
        if effort:
            argv += ["--effort", effort]
        try:
            with open(log, "ab") as out:
                proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=cwd, start_new_session=True, stdout=out,
                                        stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=child_env(repo))
        except OSError as err:
            return failed(record, f"cannot launch {argv[0]}: {err.strerror or err}")
        record["pid"] = proc.pid
    else:
        name = f"{repo.name} #{n} {ticket.get('title') or ''}".strip()
        argv = [claude_exe(), "--bg", "-n", name, "--permission-mode", "auto"]
        if effort:
            argv += ["--effort", effort]
        argv.append(prompt)
        try:
            done = subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace",
                                  stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=LAUNCH_TIMEOUT, env=child_env(repo))
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as err:
            return failed(record, f"cannot launch {argv[0]} --bg: {err}")
        try:
            with open(log, "a", encoding="utf-8") as out:
                out.write(done.stdout + done.stderr)
        except OSError:
            pass
        m = BG_ID_RE.search(done.stdout + "\n" + done.stderr)
        if done.returncode != 0 or not m:
            why = last_line(done.stderr) or last_line(done.stdout) or f"exit {done.returncode}"
            return failed(record, f"claude --bg gave no session id: {why}")
        record["bg_id"] = m.group(1)
    save_run(record)
    return record


def started_comments(repo, n):
    """How many "Started on" comments ticket n carries."""
    issue = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "view", str(n), "--json", "comments"])
    comments = issue.get("comments") if isinstance(issue, dict) else None
    return sum(1 for c in comments or [] if isinstance(c, dict) and str(c.get("body") or "").startswith("Started on"))


def start_wait():
    try:
        return max(0.0, float(os.environ.get("HARNESS_START_WAIT", START_WAIT)))
    except ValueError:
        return START_WAIT


def stop_launched(record):
    """Stop the session of a launch that never started (a bg session by `claude stop`, a headless run by a signal to
    its process group, started with start_new_session); a clause for the error line saying what happened."""
    if is_bg(record):
        bg_id = str(record.get("bg_id"))
        why = stop_bg(record)
        return f"stopped session {bg_id}" if why is None else f"could not stop session {bg_id}: {why}"
    pid = record.get("pid")
    if not pid_alive(pid, parse_iso(record.get("started_at"))):
        return "it had exited"
    try:
        os.killpg(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return "it had exited"
    except OSError as err:
        return f"could not stop pid {pid}: {err.strerror or err}"
    return f"stopped pid {pid}"


def confirm_started(repo, pending):
    """Wait together, up to HARNESS_START_WAIT seconds (default 60) in all, for each launched session's own
    `harness-work start` to comment "Started on" (more such comments than `before`, counted ahead of its launch).
    `pending` is a list of (record, before); `before` None: nothing to compare. Returns {ticket: why} for those that
    did not start (#367). A session still running that never posts is stopped and its record ends in error, so the
    next dispatch retries the ticket. A headless run that exited without one is left unended: the sweep classifies
    its log (a billing or auth failure marks the api budget and does not count toward the redispatch cap)."""
    wait = start_wait()
    waiting = [(record, before) for record, before in pending if before is not None]
    bad, deadline = {}, time.monotonic() + wait
    while waiting:
        for item in list(waiting):
            record, before = item
            n = record["ticket"]
            gone = not is_bg(record) and not pid_alive(record.get("pid"), parse_iso(record.get("started_at")))
            try:
                seen = started_comments(repo, n) > before   # read after `gone`: a comment just before exit counts
            except Problem:
                seen = False                                # a failed read is "not yet"; the deadline decides
            if seen:
                waiting.remove(item)
            elif gone:
                waiting.remove(item)
                bad[n] = (f"the session exited before it posted \"Started on\" on #{n}; its run record is left "
                          f"for the sweep to classify")
        left = deadline - time.monotonic()
        if not waiting or left <= 0:
            break
        time.sleep(min(1.0, left))
    for record, _ in waiting:
        n = record["ticket"]
        why = (f"the session did not start within {wait:g} s (no \"Started on\" comment on #{n}); "
               f"{stop_launched(record)}")
        end_failed(record, why)
        bad[n] = one_line(why)
    return bad


def end_failed(record, why):
    record.update(ended_at=iso(now()), outcome="error", error=one_line(why))
    save_run(record)


def failed(record, why):
    """A launch that never ran: recorded as ended in error, so the next dispatch picks the ticket up again."""
    end_failed(record, why)
    raise Problem(why)


def on_pty(argv, cwd, env, timeout):
    """(exit code, output) of `argv` with its stdout and stderr on a pseudo-terminal and stdin on /dev/null: the
    output without ANSI escapes, carriage returns and other control characters; the exit code None when it ran past
    `timeout` seconds and was killed. Problem when it cannot start."""
    master, slave = pty.openpty()
    try:
        fcntl.ioctl(slave, termios.TIOCSWINSZ, struct.pack("HHHH", CLOUD_WINSIZE[0], CLOUD_WINSIZE[1], 0, 0))
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=cwd, env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=slave, stderr=slave,
                                start_new_session=True)
    except OSError as err:
        os.close(master)
        raise Problem(f"cannot launch {argv[0]}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    finally:
        os.close(slave)
    chunks, deadline, timed_out = [], time.monotonic() + timeout, False
    try:
        while True:
            left = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if left <= 0:
                timed_out = True
                break
            if not select.select([master], [], [], min(left, 1.0))[0]:
                if proc.poll() is not None:             # exited, while something it started holds the terminal
                    break
                continue
            try:
                data = os.read(master, 65536)
            except OSError:                             # EIO: every writer has closed the terminal
                break
            if not data:
                break
            chunks.append(data)
    finally:
        os.close(master)
    if timed_out:
        proc.kill()
    try:
        code = proc.wait(timeout=10)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        proc.kill()
        code = proc.wait()
    text = ANSI_RE.sub("", b"".join(chunks).decode("utf-8", errors="replace")).replace("\r", "")
    return (None if timed_out else code), CONTROL_RE.sub("", text)


def cloud_prompt(slug, ticket, verify, context):
    """The whole instruction a cloud session gets: it loads no harness plugin, so nothing else tells it how to work."""
    n, branch = ticket["number"], ticket["branch"]
    api = f"repos/{slug}/issues/{n}/comments"
    check = f"`{verify}`" if verify else "that the project's CLAUDE.md names"
    return f"""Work ticket #{n} of the GitHub repository {slug} on the branch {branch}, as a plain worker. The harness \
plugin, its hooks, skills and tools (harness-board, harness-pr, harness-red) are not loaded here and nothing enforces \
tests first, so this prompt is the whole process. Review, the pull request, CI and landing happen later on the \
owner's Mac.

1. First check that `git remote get-url origin` works and that `git push --dry-run origin {branch}` succeeds. If \
either fails, stop and say so: a session cloned from a seed bundle (no Claude GitHub integration) can never push.
2. Stay on {branch}: never commit to, push or merge main, and open no pull request.
3. Tests first: write the tests the ticket names, run them and see them fail, then change the source until they pass. \
Never delete, skip or loosen a test.
4. Run the verify command {check} until it passes, commit with a message that names #{n}, and push {branch} to origin.
5. `gh issue` and `gh pr` do not work here (GraphQL is blocked); use `gh api` REST. Read the ticket's comments with \
`gh api {api}`; comment with `gh api {api} -F body=@<file>`.
6. Done and pushed: comment with `{CLOUD_DONE}` as the first line, then what changed, the tail of the verify output \
and one `Ruling: <choice>, because <reason>` line per choice you made that the ticket left open.
7. Blocked by a question about product behavior, something hard to undo, or security, credentials or personal data: \
push what you have, then comment with `{CLOUD_BLOCKED}` as the first line and the question on the lines after it, \
and stop. Do not guess.

The ticket:

{context.strip()}
"""


def launch_cloud(repo, ticket, prompt):
    """`claude --cloud <prompt> --on-branch <branch>` for a started, pushed ticket, on a pseudo-terminal; the run
    record (venue cloud, cloud_id, url). A failure, or output without a session URL, ends the record in error; billing
    wording there marks the cloud budget exhausted."""
    n = ticket["number"]
    started = now()
    rid = f"{repo.key}-{n}-{started.strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M%S')}"
    log = os.path.join(runs_dir(), f"{rid}.log")
    os.makedirs(runs_dir(), exist_ok=True)
    record = {"id": rid, "ticket": n, "repo": repo.main, "worktree": ticket["worktree"], "branch": ticket["branch"],
              "venue": "cloud", "log": log, "started_at": iso(started), "ended_at": None, "exit": None,
              "outcome": None}
    argv = [claude_exe(), "--cloud", prompt, "--on-branch", ticket["branch"]]
    try:
        code, text = on_pty(argv, ticket["worktree"], child_env(), CLOUD_TIMEOUT)
    except Problem as err:
        failed(record, str(err))
    try:
        with open(log, "a", encoding="utf-8") as out:
            out.write(text)
    except OSError:
        pass
    found = CLOUD_URL_RE.search(text)
    if code != 0 or found is None:
        lines = [line.strip() for line in text.splitlines() if line.strip()]
        last = lines[-1] if lines else ""
        if code is None:
            why = f"claude --cloud timed out after {CLOUD_TIMEOUT} s" + (f": {last}" if last else "")
        elif code != 0:
            why = f"claude --cloud failed: {last or f'exit {code}'}"
        else:
            why = f"claude --cloud started no session: {last or 'no output'}"
        billing = matched_line(lines, CLOUD_BILLING_RE)
        if billing:
            exhaust(load_budgets(), "cloud", f"billing: {billing}", EXHAUST_HOURS)
            why += f"; the cloud budget is marked exhausted for {EXHAUST_HOURS:g} h"
        failed(record, why)
    record.update(cloud_id=found.group(1), url=found.group(0))
    save_run(record)
    return record


ISSUES = {}         # (main checkout, ticket): the issue or the Problem, read once per command
WITHOUT_PR = {}     # (main checkout, ticket, branch): the issue, None or the Problem, asked once per command
PR_ROWS = 100       # pull requests of a branch read by ask_without_pr


def ticket_issue(repo, n):
    """Ticket n's issue (number, title, state, stateReason, labels); a failing gh call raises Problem. One command reads
    each issue once: the sweep's finished and early checks, dispatch's redispatch and the branch judge share it, a
    failure included."""
    key = (repo.main, n)
    if key not in ISSUES:
        try:
            ISSUES[key] = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "view", str(n), "--json", "number,title,state,stateReason,labels"])
        except Problem as err:
            ISSUES[key] = err
    found = ISSUES[key]
    if isinstance(found, Problem):
        raise found
    return found


def without_pr(repo, n, branch):
    """The issue of ticket n when it is OPEN and status:in-progress and `branch` has no ready pull request in any
    state (none, or only drafts), else None; its `draft_pr` is the newest open draft's number, or None. A failing
    gh call raises Problem. One command asks gh once per ticket and branch: dispatch's sweep
    and its redispatch share the answer, a failure included."""
    key = (repo.main, n, branch)
    if key not in WITHOUT_PR:
        try:
            WITHOUT_PR[key] = ask_without_pr(repo, n, branch)
        except Problem as err:
            WITHOUT_PR[key] = err
    found = WITHOUT_PR[key]
    if isinstance(found, Problem):
        raise found
    return found


def branch_prs(repo, branch, strict=False):
    """The pull requests of `branch` in any state, newest first (a failing gh call raises Problem; with `strict` so
    does an answer that is not a list, which otherwise reads as none)."""
    prs = gh_json(repo, ["pr", "list", "--head", str(branch), "--state", "all", "--json", "number,state,isDraft",
                         "--limit", str(PR_ROWS)]) if branch else []
    if strict and not isinstance(prs, list):
        raise Problem(f"gh pr list --head {branch} printed no list of pull requests")
    return [pr for pr in prs if isinstance(pr, dict)] if isinstance(prs, list) else []


def resume_state(repo, branch, worktree):
    """(resume, pr) of a started ticket: `pr` is the newest open pull request of the branch (a draft counts), else
    None; `resume` is true when there is such a PR or the branch carries commits beyond origin/main (main without an
    origin), false on a fresh start."""
    opened = [pr.get("number") for pr in branch_prs(repo, branch) if str(pr.get("state", "")).upper() == "OPEN"]
    pr = opened[0] if opened else None
    base = next((ref for ref in ("origin/main", "main") if ref_exists(repo, ref)), None)
    ahead = git(worktree, "rev-list", "--count", f"{base}..HEAD") if base else None
    commits = ahead is not None and ahead.returncode == 0 and ahead.stdout.strip() not in ("", "0")
    return pr is not None or commits, pr


def ask_without_pr(repo, n, branch):
    issue = ticket_issue(repo, n)
    if not isinstance(issue, dict) or str(issue.get("state", "")).upper() != "OPEN":
        return None
    labels = [lb.get("name") for lb in issue.get("labels") or [] if isinstance(lb, dict)]
    if "status:in-progress" not in labels:
        return None
    rows = branch_prs(repo, branch)
    if any(pr.get("isDraft") is not True for pr in rows):    # a ready one, merged or closed too: a normal end
        return None
    drafts = [pr.get("number") for pr in rows if str(pr.get("state", "")).upper() == "OPEN"]   # newest first
    return dict(issue, draft_pr=drafts[0] if drafts else None)


def redispatch_candidates(repo, records, live, *, capped_only=False, only=None):
    """In-progress tickets whose last run ended (within the window) without a ready pull request: dispatched again,
    unless REDISPATCH_MAX runs of the ticket ended within the window, billing and auth runs not counting (the
    budget's failure, not the ticket's). (candidates, skipped, the id of the record each skipped ticket's cap rests
    on: its latest started). `capped_only` skips the gh check for tickets under the cap, whose answer the caller
    would discard. `only` (a set of ticket numbers) considers just those tickets."""
    cutoff = now() - REDISPATCH_WINDOW
    latest, ended_runs = {}, {}
    for record in records:
        n = record.get("ticket")
        if not isinstance(n, int):
            continue
        if only is not None and n not in only:
            continue
        if n not in latest or str(record.get("started_at")) > str(latest[n].get("started_at")):
            latest[n] = record
        ended = parse_iso(record.get("ended_at"))
        if ended is not None and ended >= cutoff and record.get("outcome") not in UNCOUNTED:
            ended_runs[n] = ended_runs.get(n, 0) + 1
    out, skipped, capped_ids = [], [], {}
    for n, record in sorted(latest.items()):
        ended = parse_iso(record.get("ended_at"))
        if n in live or ended is None or ended < cutoff:
            continue
        if capped_only and ended_runs.get(n, 0) < REDISPATCH_MAX:
            continue
        try:
            issue = without_pr(repo, n, record.get("branch"))
        except Problem as err:
            warn(f"#{n}: cannot check whether its ended run needs another: {err}")
            continue
        if issue is None:
            continue
        again = record.get("outcome") or "ended"
        if ended_runs.get(n, 0) >= REDISPATCH_MAX:
            days = REDISPATCH_WINDOW.days
            skipped.append({"number": n, "why": f"{ended_runs[n]} runs ended without a ready pull request in {days} "
                                                f"days (last: {again} at {record.get('ended_at')}); run it in this "
                                                f"session with /harness:work {n}, or wait for the window",
                            "runs": ended_runs[n], "window_days": days, "advice": f"/harness:work {n}"})
            capped_ids[n] = record.get("id")
            continue
        out.append({"number": n, "title": issue.get("title") or "", "tier": None, "again": again,
                    "draft_pr": issue.get("draft_pr")})
    return out, skipped, capped_ids


def live_runs(records, agents):
    """{ticket: its first live record} among `records`."""
    live = {}
    for record in records:
        if isinstance(record.get("ticket"), int) and run_live(record, agents):
            live.setdefault(record["ticket"], record)
    return live


# --------------------------------------------------------------- commands
def cmd_start(repo, args):
    ticket = start_ticket(repo, args.number, args.venue, announce=True)
    context = board(repo, "show", args.number, "--markdown").rstrip("\n")
    data = {"number": ticket["number"], "branch": ticket["branch"], "worktree": ticket["worktree"],
            "tier": ticket["tier"], "previous_status": ticket["previous_status"], "waiting": ticket["waiting"],
            "answers": ticket["answers"], "context": context}
    if ticket["type"] == "ops":
        data.update(ops=True, before_dir=ticket["before_dir"], resume=False, pr=None)
        text = (f"Ops ticket: no branch or worktree; save the before-values in {ticket['before_dir']} before any "
                f"write.\n\n{context}")
    else:
        data["resume"], data["pr"] = resume_state(repo, ticket["branch"], ticket["worktree"])
        text = f"{ticket['worktree']}\n\n{context}"
    if data["resume"]:
        where = f"open PR #{data['pr']}" if data["pr"] else "commits and no open PR"
        text += f"\n\nResume: {ticket['branch']} already has {where}; pick up where it stopped, not at the tests."
    if ticket["waiting"]:
        text += f"\n\n#{ticket['number']} is status:needs-input with no answer yet; its status is unchanged."
    elif ticket["answers"]:
        bodies = [str(a.get("body") or "").strip() if isinstance(a, dict) else str(a) for a in ticket["answers"]]
        text += "\n\n## Answers\n\n" + "\n\n".join(b for b in bodies if b)
    emit(wants_json(args), data, text)


def cmd_cloud(repo, args):
    n = args.number
    until = exhausted_until(load_budgets()["cloud"])
    if until:
        raise Problem(f"the cloud budget is exhausted until {iso(until)}; nothing started. Run #{n} here with "
                      f"/harness:work {n}, or `harness-work budget reset cloud` once cloud sessions work again")
    unended = [r for r in load_runs() if r.get("ticket") == n and is_cloud(r) and not r.get("ended_at")
               and of_repo(r, repo)]
    if unended:
        raise Problem(f"#{n} already has a cloud run that has not ended: {unended[0].get('id')} "
                      f"({unended[0].get('url')}); follow it with harness-work runs --sweep")
    labels = issue_labels(repo, n)
    if "needs-local" in labels or "ops" in labels:
        what = "an ops ticket" if "ops" in labels else "labelled needs-local"
        raise Problem(f"#{n} is {what}: it needs this machine; run it here with /harness:work {n}")
    if "status:needs-input" in labels and not board_json(repo, "answers", n, "--json"):
        raise Problem(f"#{n} is status:needs-input with no answer since its question; nothing started. Answer it "
                      f"on the ticket, then run harness-work cloud {n} again")
    if shutil.which(claude_exe()) is None:
        raise Problem(f"claude not found ({claude_exe()}); nothing started")
    found = gh_json(repo, ["repo", "view", "--json", "nameWithOwner"])
    slug = found.get("nameWithOwner") if isinstance(found, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(slug, str) or "/" not in slug:
        raise Problem("gh repo view printed no owner/name; nothing started")
    file_env, foreign = settings_env(repo.main), other_project(repo.main)
    verify = (project_setting("CLAUDE_VERIFY_CMD", file_env, foreign)
              or project_setting("HARNESS_TEST_CMD", file_env, foreign))
    ticket = start_ticket(repo, n, "cloud")
    branch = ticket["branch"]
    pushed = git(ticket["worktree"], "push", "-u", "origin", branch)
    if pushed.returncode != 0:
        why = last_line(pushed.stderr) or f"exit {pushed.returncode}"
        raise Problem(f"git push of {branch} to origin failed ({why}); no cloud session launched")
    context = board(repo, "show", n, "--markdown")
    record = launch_cloud(repo, ticket, cloud_prompt(slug, ticket, verify, context))
    try:
        board(repo, "comment", n, "--body", f"Cloud session on {branch}: {record['url']}")
    except Problem as err:
        warn(f"#{n}: cannot comment the session URL on the ticket: {err}")
    emit(wants_json(args), record, f"#{n} cloud on {branch} ({record['url']})\nFollow it with `harness-work runs "
                                   f"--sweep`; once it is done, bring it home here with /harness:work {n}.")


def stage_route(repo, cache, stage):
    """(route tier, route effort, default tier) for `stage`: the route harness_lib.routing gives it from the cache's
    labels and the current settings (review_route for review, code_route for every other stage), and the tier an
    attempt without --tier ran at. That is the route's tier, except that a coding stage keeps a cached sonnet or opus
    (the effective tier harness-board wrote); a cached fable is the pre-#239 rubric's and yields to the route. A
    cache without labels routes from its cached tier (opus when it has none) as `harness-board tier` does
    (cached_code_route: a cached fable reads as opus xhigh, and the code settings still decide); the review stage
    reads it the same way without the code settings."""
    cached = cache.get("tier") if cache.get("tier") in TIERS else None
    labels = cache.get("labels")
    routing = load_routing(repo.main)
    for problem in routing["problems"]:
        warn(problem)
    if not isinstance(labels, list):
        route = cached_code_route(cached or DEFAULT_TIER, {} if stage == "review" else routing)
        return route["tier"], route["effort"], route["tier"]
    names = [x.get("name") if isinstance(x, dict) else x for x in labels]
    kind = cost.label_fields([x for x in names if isinstance(x, str)])
    if stage == "review":
        route = review_route(kind["risk"], routing)
    else:
        route = code_route(kind["type"], kind["size"], kind["risk"], routing)
        if cached in ("sonnet", "opus"):
            return route["tier"], route["effort"], cached
    return route["tier"], route["effort"], route["tier"]


def ticket_cache(repo, n):
    cache = read_cache(repo, n)
    if cache is None:
        raise Problem(f"no ticket cache for #{n} ({repo.ticket_path(n)}); run harness-work start {n} first")
    return cache


def record_attempt(repo, cache, args):
    """Append args' attempt to ticket args.number's cache `cache`, write it and return the failure policy's answer
    as attempt's --json object. attempt and stage both record through here."""
    n = args.number
    route_tier, route_effort, default_tier = stage_route(repo, cache, args.stage)
    tier = args.tier or default_tier
    effort = args.effort or (route_effort if tier == route_tier else None)
    attempts = cache.get("attempts") if isinstance(cache.get("attempts"), list) else []
    attempts.append({"stage": args.stage, "tier": tier, "effort": effort, "result": args.result, "at": iso(now())})
    cache["attempts"] = attempts
    write_json(repo.ticket_path(n), cache)
    failures = 0
    for entry in reversed([a for a in attempts if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get("stage") == args.stage]):
        if entry.get("result") != "fail":
            break
        failures += 1
    action = cost.attempt_action(args.stage, args.result, failures)     # fix: two rounds, never escalate; breaker: done
    nxt = next_route(tier, effort) if action == "escalate" else None
    if action == "escalate" and nxt is None:
        action = "park"                 # nothing above opus xhigh or an explicit fable
    next_tier, next_effort = nxt or (None, None)
    return {"number": n, "stage": args.stage, "result": args.result, "tier": tier, "effort": effort,
            "failures": failures, "action": action, "next_tier": next_tier, "next_effort": next_effort}


def answer_text(data):
    """attempt's text answer: `done`, `retry`, `escalate <tier> [<effort>]` or `park`."""
    return " ".join(x for x in (data["action"], data["next_tier"], data["next_effort"]) if x)


def cmd_attempt(repo, args):
    data = record_attempt(repo, ticket_cache(repo, args.number), args)
    emit(wants_json(args), data, answer_text(data))


def ticket_marks(cache):
    """The cache's label names and flags, plus `risk:<risk>` from its risk: where stage reads risk:high and
    no-tests."""
    labels = cache.get("labels") if isinstance(cache.get("labels"), list) else []
    flags = cache.get("flags") if isinstance(cache.get("flags"), list) else []
    marks = [x.get("name") if isinstance(x, dict) else x for x in labels] + flags
    if isinstance(cache.get("risk"), str):
        marks.append("risk:" + cache["risk"])
    return {m for m in marks if isinstance(m, str)}


def stage_refusal(n, stage, result, marks, found):
    """Why `stage` must not record this attempt, or None. `found` is the latest review round's blocking count
    (None without a round), read for review and fix only."""
    if stage in ("tests", "breaker") and "no-tests" in marks:
        return f"#{n} is flagged no-tests; it has no {stage} stage"
    if stage == "breaker" and "risk:high" not in marks:
        return f"#{n} is not risk:high; the breaker runs only on risk:high tickets"
    if stage not in ("review", "fix"):
        return None
    if found is None:
        return f"no review round recorded for #{n}; run harness-pr findings first"
    if stage == "fix" and (result == "pass") == (found > 0):
        findings = f"{found} blocking finding" + ("" if found == 1 else "s")
        return (f"fix {result} on #{n}: its latest review round has {findings}; "
                f"fix {result} needs {'none' if result == 'pass' else 'at least one'}")
    return None


def next_step(data, marks, found):
    """The work loop's step after the attempt `data`: the same stage on retry or escalate, park, or the
    stage done leads to (a breaker failure is done: code, with the gaps as requirements)."""
    stage, action = data["stage"], data["action"]
    if action == "park":
        return "park"
    if action != "done":
        return stage
    if stage in ("review", "fix"):
        return "fix" if found else "ci"
    high = "risk:high" in marks
    return {"tests": "breaker" if high else "code", "breaker": "code", "code": "review",
            "ci": "ultra, then ready" if high else "ready"}[stage]


def cmd_stage(repo, args):
    n = args.number
    cache = ticket_cache(repo, n)
    marks = ticket_marks(cache)
    found = None
    if args.stage in ("review", "fix"):
        rnd = reviews.latest_round(repo.key, n)
        found = None if rnd is None else len(reviews.blocking(rnd))
    why = stage_refusal(n, args.stage, args.result, marks, found)
    if why:
        raise Problem(why)
    data = record_attempt(repo, cache, args)
    data["next"] = next_step(data, marks, found)
    emit(wants_json(args), data, f"{answer_text(data)}\nnext: {data['next']}")


PR_FIELDS = "number,url,createdAt,mergedAt,headRefName"
RUN_FIELDS = "databaseId,status,conclusion,createdAt,startedAt,updatedAt"


def gh_part(repo, args, shape):
    """gh's JSON for one part of the cost record, or None with one warning line naming the call when gh fails or
    prints something other than a `shape`."""
    try:
        data = gh_json(repo, args)
    except Problem as err:
        warn(str(err))
        return None
    if not isinstance(data, shape):
        warn(f"gh {' '.join(args[:2])} printed no {'list' if shape is list else 'object'}")
        return None
    return data


def cost_extras(repo, record, cache):
    """Fill the record's gh-backed parts in place: the PR (--pr, else the branch's), its lines, its CI runs, the
    ticket's needs-input count, the elapsed times and the labels the cache lacks. A failed call leaves its part
    null."""
    n, pr = record["ticket"], record["pr"]
    branch = cache.get("branch") if cache and isinstance(cache.get("branch"), str) else None
    info = None
    if pr is not None:
        info = gh_part(repo, ["pr", "view", str(pr), "--json", PR_FIELDS], dict)
    elif branch:
        found = gh_part(repo, ["pr", "list", "--head", branch, "--state", "all", "--json", PR_FIELDS,
                               "--limit", "10"], list)
        info = cost.pick_pr(found)
        pr = record["pr"] = info["number"] if info else None
    info = info or {}
    if pr is not None:
        file_env = settings_env(repo.main, ("settings.json",))
        globs = [patterns(setting(name, file_env) or default) for name, default in
                 (("HARNESS_TEST_PATTERNS", DEFAULT_TEST_PATTERNS), ("HARNESS_SOURCE_EXEMPT", DEFAULT_SOURCE_EXEMPT))]
        pages = gh_part(repo, ["api", f"repos/{{owner}}/{{repo}}/pulls/{pr}/files?per_page=100", "--paginate",
                               "--slurp"], list)
        if pages is not None:
            record["lines"] = cost.line_counts(pages, *globs)
        head = info.get("headRefName") if isinstance(info.get("headRefName"), str) else branch
        if head:
            runs = gh_part(repo, ["run", "list", "--branch", head, "--json", RUN_FIELDS, "--limit", "100"], list)
            if runs is not None:
                record["ci"] = cost.ci_summary(runs)
    issue = gh_part(repo, ["issue", "view", str(n), "--json", "comments,labels"], dict)
    comments = issue.get("comments") if issue and isinstance(issue.get("comments"), list) else None
    if issue is not None:
        record["needs_input"] = cost.needs_input_count(comments)
        labels = issue.get("labels") if isinstance(issue.get("labels"), list) else []
        names = [x.get("name") if isinstance(x, dict) else x for x in labels]
        for key, value in cost.label_fields([x for x in names if isinstance(x, str)]).items():
            if record[key] is None:
                record[key] = value
    started = (cache.get("started_at") if cache else None) or cost.started_from_comments(comments)
    ready = cost.ready_from_comments(comments, pr) if pr is not None else None
    landed = info.get("mergedAt") or None
    record["elapsed"] = cost.elapsed(started, info.get("createdAt") or None, ready, landed)
    record["landed_at"] = landed


def cmd_cost(repo, args):
    """Ticket N's tokens and model time per stage and model, from the transcripts and the ticket cache:
    saved as cost/<N>.json (replacing an earlier record), printed as text, --json or --markdown."""
    n = args.number
    usage = cost.ticket_usage(repo.main, n)
    cache = read_cache(repo, n)
    record = cost.build_record(n, repo.main, usage, cache, args.pr, iso(now()))
    cost_extras(repo, record, cache)
    path = repo.cost_path(n)
    write_json(path, record)
    if args.markdown:
        print(cost.render_markdown(record))
    else:
        emit(wants_json(args), record, f"{cost.render_text(record)}\nSaved {path}")


def after_tickets(n, ready, live):
    """--after N: (the tickets to dispatch as --only would, the `after` record). The ready tickets whose blockers
    include N, else the first ready ticket in ready's order without a live run, else none."""
    unblocked = [r["number"] for r in ready if isinstance(r.get("number"), int)
                 and n in (r.get("blocked_by") if isinstance(r.get("blocked_by"), list) else [])]
    nxt = None
    if not unblocked:
        nxt = next((r["number"] for r in ready if isinstance(r.get("number"), int) and r["number"] not in live),
                   None)
    return (unblocked or ([nxt] if nxt is not None else [])), {"ticket": n, "unblocked": unblocked, "next": nxt}


def after_text(after):
    if after["unblocked"]:
        return f"after #{after['ticket']}: {', '.join(f'#{n}' for n in after['unblocked'])} unblocked"
    if after["next"] is not None:
        return f"after #{after['ticket']}: none unblocked; next ready #{after['next']}"
    return f"after #{after['ticket']}: nothing ready"


def is_ops(repo, row):
    """Whether a dispatch candidate is an ops ticket: its ready row's type, else its ticket cache's."""
    kind = row.get("type") or (read_cache(repo, row["number"]) or {}).get("type")
    return kind == "ops"


def answered_needs_input(repo, n):
    """Ticket n is status:needs-input and the owner has answered since its question (harness-board answers)."""
    try:
        if "status:needs-input" not in issue_labels(repo, n):
            return False
        return bool(board_json(repo, "answers", n, "--json"))
    except Problem:
        return False


def routing_of(repo):
    """load_routing for the main checkout, each problem warned once and remembered in REPORTED."""
    routing = load_routing(repo.main)
    for problem in routing["problems"]:
        warn(problem)
        REPORTED.add(one_line(problem))
    return routing


def cmd_dispatch(repo, args):
    if args.max < 1:
        raise Problem("--max must be at least 1")
    routing = routing_of(repo)       # once per dispatch, whatever the run does next
    agents = Agents()
    records = load_runs()
    sweep(records, agents, wants_json(args), dry_run=args.dry_run)
    api_until = exhausted_until(load_budgets()["api"])    # after the sweep, which can be what exhausts it
    if args.venue == "headless" and api_until:
        raise Problem(f"the api budget is exhausted until {iso(api_until)}; nothing started. Dispatch "
                      f"without --api or --venue headless to run on the subscription, or `harness-work budget reset "
                      f"api` once the api key works again")
    if args.venue != "headless":
        subscription_hold()         # after the sweep too, which can be what exhausts it
    data, failed_any = dispatch_repo(repo, args, routing, records, agents)
    if args.json:
        emit(True, data, "")
    if failed_any:
        sys.exit(1)


def dispatch_repo(repo, args, routing, records, agents, shared=None):
    """One repository's dispatch after the sweep and the budget checks: plan, start and launch, printing its text
    lines (none under --json). (the --json result, whether a launch failed). `shared` is --all-projects' (live runs
    across every project, slots left) in place of this repository's live runs and --max minus them."""
    effort = routing["code_effort"]
    mine = [r for r in records if of_repo(r, repo)]
    venue = args.venue or "bg"
    live = live_runs(mine, agents)
    live_count, slots = (len(live), args.max - len(live)) if shared is None else shared

    def done(data, text):
        if not args.json:
            print(text)
        return data, False

    ready = board_json(repo, "ready", "--json")
    ready = [r for r in ready if isinstance(r, dict)] if isinstance(ready, list) else []
    named, after = args.only, None
    if args.after is not None:      # --only's path, with the tickets N unblocked, else the next ready one
        named, after = after_tickets(args.after, ready, live)
    only = set(named) if named is not None else None
    again, capped, _ = redispatch_candidates(repo, mine, live, only=only)
    candidates, seen = [], set()
    for row in again + ready:
        n = row.get("number")
        if isinstance(n, int) and n not in seen and (only is None or n in only):
            seen.add(n)
            candidates.append(row)
    plan, skipped = [], list(capped)
    for n in named or []:           # a named ticket that is no candidate: say why, launch nothing for it
        if n in seen or any(s["number"] == n for s in skipped):
            continue
        seen.add(n)
        if n not in live and answered_needs_input(repo, n):     # the owner's answer resumes it, as cloud does (#367)
            candidates.append({"number": n, "title": "", "again": "an answer to its question"})
            continue
        skipped.append({"number": n, "why": f"live run {live[n]['id']}" if n in live else
                        "not ready, and not in progress with an ended run to redispatch"})
    kept_local = []                 # ops tickets a headless dispatch leaves out: they need this Mac's connectors
    for row in candidates:
        if row["number"] in live:
            skipped.append({"number": row["number"], "why": f"live run {live[row['number']]['id']}"})
        elif venue == "headless" and is_ops(repo, row):
            kept_local.append({"number": row["number"], "why": f"an ops ticket needs this Mac's connectors and "
                                                               f"credentials, never headless; dispatch it bg or run "
                                                               f"/harness:work {row['number']} here"})
            skipped.append(kept_local[-1])
        elif len(plan) < slots or not args.dry_run:
            plan.append(row)
        else:
            skipped.append({"number": row["number"], "why": f"over --max {args.max}"})

    def describe(row):
        detail = f"tier {row['tier']}" if row.get("tier") else f"again after {row.get('again')}"
        if row.get("draft_pr"):
            detail += f", draft PR #{row['draft_pr']}"
        return f"#{row['number']} {row.get('title') or ''} ({detail})"

    wave_tier = routing["wave_tier"]
    extra = {"wave": None} if wave_tier else {}     # without HARNESS_WAVE_REVIEW the output is as before #180
    if after is not None:
        extra["after"] = after
    if args.dry_run:
        shown = f"effort {effort}, " if effort else ""
        lines = [f"Dry run: venue {venue}, {shown}{live_count} live, {max(0, slots)} of {args.max} slots free."]
        lines += [after_text(after)] if after is not None else []
        lines += [f"would start {describe(row)} and launch {venue}" for row in plan]
        group = [row["number"] for row in plan if open_wave(repo, row["number"]) is None] if wave_tier else []
        if group:
            lines.append(f"would group {tickets_text(group)} into a wave")
            extra["wave"] = {"id": None, "tickets": sorted(group)}
        lines += [f"skip #{s['number']}: {s['why']}" for s in skipped]
        if not candidates:
            lines.append("None of the named tickets can be planned." if args.only else "No ready tickets.")
        return done(dict({"venue": venue, "effort": effort, "dry_run": True, "live": [r["id"] for r in live.values()],
                          "plan": plan, "skipped": skipped}, **extra), "\n".join(lines))
    if not args.json:
        if after is not None:
            print(after_text(after), flush=True)
        for s in (skipped if only is not None else capped + kept_local):
            print(f"skip #{s['number']}: {s['why']}", flush=True)
    if not candidates:
        return done(dict({"venue": venue, "effort": effort, "launched": [], "failed": [], "skipped": skipped},
                         **extra),
                    "None of the named tickets can be launched." if args.only else "No ready tickets.")
    if slots <= 0:
        return done(dict({"venue": venue, "effort": effort, "launched": [], "failed": [], "skipped": skipped},
                         **extra),
                    f"{live_count} live runs; --max {args.max} reached, nothing launched.")
    if not plan:
        return done(dict({"venue": venue, "effort": effort, "launched": [], "failed": [], "skipped": skipped},
                         **extra),
                    "Nothing to launch: " + "; ".join([f"#{s['number']} has a {s['why']}" for s in skipped
                                                       if s not in capped and s["why"].startswith("live run")]
                                                      + [f"#{s['number']} is {s['why']}" for s in kept_local]) + ".")
    if shutil.which(claude_exe()) is None:
        raise Problem(f"claude not found ({claude_exe()}); nothing started")
    # launch every planned session first, then wait for all of them together (#367): the wait stays near
    # HARNESS_START_WAIT instead of that long for each launch in turn
    outcomes, pending = [], []
    for row in plan:
        if sum(1 for _, rec, _ in outcomes if rec is not None) >= slots:
            break
        n = row["number"]
        try:
            ticket = start_ticket(repo, n, venue, row.get("draft_pr"))
            if not ticket["title"]:
                ticket["title"] = row.get("title") or ""
            route = code_route(ticket["type"], ticket["size"], ticket["risk"], routing)
            try:
                before = started_comments(repo, n)
            except Problem:
                before = None
            record = launch(repo, ticket, venue, route["effort"])
        except Problem as err:
            outcomes.append((n, None, one_line(err)))
            continue
        outcomes.append((n, record, None))
        pending.append((record, before))
    not_started = confirm_started(repo, pending)
    launched, failures = [], []
    named = f"{repo.name} " if shared is not None else ""     # --all-projects: the stderr line names the project
    for n, record, why in outcomes:
        why = why or not_started.get(n)
        if why:
            failures.append({"number": n, "error": why})
            if not args.json:
                print(f"{named}#{n} not launched: {why}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            continue
        launched.append(record)
        if not args.json:
            where = f"pid {record['pid']}, log {record['log']}" if venue == "headless" else f"id {record['bg_id']}"
            print(f"#{n} {venue} on {record['branch'] or 'the main checkout (ops)'} ({where})", flush=True)
    if wave_tier and launched:
        extra["wave"] = group_wave(repo, launched, wave_tier, routing["wave_effort"], args.json)
    return (dict({"venue": venue, "effort": effort, "launched": launched, "failed": failures, "skipped": skipped},
                 **extra), bool(failures))


def autodispatch_repo(project):
    """(the Repo, None) for a registered project that opted in and has no open incident; (None, why) for one that is
    skipped. Opted in: HARNESS_AUTODISPATCH is 1 (a string or a number) in the .claude/settings.json committed at
    origin/main (settings.committed_env), never the working tree, settings.local.json or this environment. A Problem
    when the project cannot be read: its folder gone, not a repository, gh failing."""
    if not os.path.isdir(project.path):
        raise Problem(f"{project.path} is not a folder (moved or removed? harness-projects lists the registry)")
    repo = Repo(project.path)
    if setting_from(AUTODISPATCH, committed_env(repo.main)) != "1":
        return None, f"not opted in ({AUTODISPATCH} is not 1 in .claude/settings.json at origin/main)"
    found = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "list", "--label", "incident", "--state", "open", "--json", "number,title"])
    incidents = [f"#{i.get('number')}" for i in found if isinstance(i, dict)] if isinstance(found, list) else []
    if incidents:
        return None, f"incident {', '.join(incidents)} open"
    return repo, None


def cmd_dispatch_all(args):
    """dispatch --all-projects (#164): one sweep of every run, the subscription hold, then each registered project in
    registry order that autodispatch_repo admits gets this repository's dispatch in the bg venue, its slots --max
    minus the live runs of every project (each live record counts) and minus what earlier projects launched. A
    skipped project is one line; a failing one is one stderr line, the rest still run, and the exit is 1 at the end.
    Needs no repository in the cwd (launchd's job has none)."""
    if args.max < 1:
        raise Problem("--max must be at least 1")
    as_json = wants_json(args)
    agents = Agents()
    records = load_runs()
    sweep(records, agents, as_json, dry_run=args.dry_run)
    subscription_hold()
    projects = load_registry()
    live = sum(1 for r in records if run_live(r, agents))
    taken, results, failed_any = 0, [], False
    if not as_json:
        print(f"All projects: {live} live, --max {args.max}" + (", dry run." if args.dry_run else "."), flush=True)
    for project in projects:
        entry = {"name": project.name, "path": project.path, "status": "dispatched", "why": None, "result": None}
        results.append(entry)
        try:
            repo, why = autodispatch_repo(project)
            if repo is None:
                entry.update(status="skipped", why=why)
                if not as_json:
                    print(f"{project.name}: skipped, {why}", flush=True)
                continue
            routing = routing_of(repo)
            if not as_json:
                print(f"{project.name} ({repo.main}):", flush=True)
            data, failed = dispatch_repo(repo, args, routing, records, agents,
                                         shared=(live + taken, args.max - live - taken))
        except Problem as err:
            entry.update(status="failed", why=one_line(err))
            print(f"harness-work: {project.name}: {one_line(err)}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            failed_any = True
            continue
        entry["result"] = data
        taken += len(data.get("plan") or []) if args.dry_run else len(data.get("launched") or [])
        failed_any = failed_any or failed
    if as_json:
        emit(True, {"all_projects": True, "venue": "bg", "max": args.max, "dry_run": args.dry_run, "live": live,
                    "projects": results}, "")
    elif not projects:
        print("No registered projects (harness-projects add registers one).")
    if failed_any:
        sys.exit(1)


def tickets_text(numbers):
    return ", ".join(f"#{n}" for n in sorted(numbers))


def open_wave(repo, n):
    """Ticket n's newest wave (waves.wave_of) while its review has not finished, else None: a redispatched ticket
    stays in that wave, and one whose wave was reviewed joins a new one."""
    wave = waves.wave_of(repo.key, n)
    review = wave.get("review") if wave else None
    if wave is None or (isinstance(review, dict) and review.get("reviewed_at")):
        return None
    return wave


def group_wave(repo, launched, tier, effort, as_json):
    """Stamp each launched run record with its wave: a ticket already in an unreviewed wave keeps it, the rest form
    one new wave (waves.create_wave), announced on stdout. The new wave's id, or None when every ticket had one."""
    kept, fresh = {}, []
    for record in launched:
        wave = open_wave(repo, record["ticket"])
        if wave is None:
            fresh.append(record)
        else:
            kept[record["id"]] = wave["id"]
    new = waves.create_wave(repo.key, repo.main, [r["ticket"] for r in fresh], tier, effort) if fresh else None
    for record in launched:
        record["wave"] = kept.get(record["id"]) or new["id"]
        save_run(record)
    if new is None:
        return None
    if not as_json:
        print(f"wave {new['id']}: {tickets_text(new['tickets'])} (reviewed together once all are in review)",
              flush=True)
    return new["id"]


def issue_status(issue):
    """The board status of a `gh issue view --json state,labels` answer: closed for a CLOSED issue, else the name
    after `status:` of its first status label, else None."""
    if not isinstance(issue, dict):
        return None
    if str(issue.get("state", "")).upper() == "CLOSED":
        return "closed"
    for label in issue.get("labels") or []:
        name = label.get("name") if isinstance(label, dict) else label
        if isinstance(name, str) and name.startswith("status:"):
            return name[len("status:"):]
    return None


def wave_detail(wave, state, prog):
    if state == "working":
        total = len(prog["done"]) + len(prog["waiting"])
        waiting = ", ".join(f"#{w['number']} ({w['status'] or 'no status'})" for w in prog["waiting"])
        return f"{len(prog['done'])} of {total} in review; waiting for {waiting}"
    review = wave.get("review") if isinstance(wave.get("review"), dict) else {}
    if state == "reviewing":
        return f"reviewing (run {review.get('run')})"
    if state == "reviewed":
        return f"reviewed {review.get('reviewed_at')}"
    return "no tickets" if state == "empty" else state


def cmd_waves(repo, args):
    """This repository's waves with their state and what each waits for, from the ticket caches; --refresh asks gh
    once per waiting ticket."""
    every = waves.load_waves(repo.key)
    numbers = sorted({n for w in every for n in w.get("tickets") or [] if isinstance(n, int)})
    statuses = waves.ticket_statuses(repo.key, numbers)
    if args.refresh:
        for n in numbers:
            if statuses[n] in waves.DONE:
                continue
            try:
                found = gh_json(repo, ["issue", "view", str(n), "--json", "state,labels"])
            except Problem as err:
                warn(f"#{n}: cannot refresh its status; the cache's stands: {err}")
                continue
            statuses[n] = issue_status(found)
    rows = []
    for wave in every:
        tickets = [n for n in wave.get("tickets") or [] if isinstance(n, int)]
        if not args.all and all(statuses.get(n) == "closed" for n in tickets):
            continue
        prog = waves.progress(wave, statuses)
        state = waves.wave_state(wave, statuses)
        rows.append(dict(wave, state=state, done=prog["done"], waiting=prog["waiting"],
                         detail=wave_detail(wave, state, prog)))
    if args.json:
        emit(True, rows, "")
    elif not rows:
        print("No waves." if args.all else "No open waves (--all lists every wave).")
    else:
        lines = [("ID", "TICKETS", "STATE", "DETAIL")]
        lines += [(r["id"], tickets_text(r.get("tickets") or []) or "-", r["state"], r["detail"]) for r in rows]
        print(table(lines))


def cmd_wave_drop(repo, args):
    wave = waves.load_wave(repo.key, args.id)
    if wave is None:
        raise Problem(f"no wave {args.id} in this repository; harness-work waves --all lists them")
    review = wave.get("review")
    if isinstance(review, dict) and review.get("launched_at"):
        raise Problem(f"wave {args.id}'s review was launched at {review['launched_at']}; nothing dropped")
    if args.number not in (wave.get("tickets") or []):
        raise Problem(f"#{args.number} is not in wave {args.id}")
    wave = waves.drop_ticket(repo.key, args.id, args.number)
    emit(wants_json(args), wave, f"dropped #{args.number} from wave {args.id}")


def cmd_runs(args):
    agents = Agents()
    records = load_runs()
    if args.sweep:
        sweep(records, agents, wants_json(args))
    cutoff = now() - RECENT
    try:                    # the tickets dispatch would skip for the cap, in the repository of the cwd
        repo = open_repo(None)
        mine = [r for r in records if of_repo(r, repo)]
        capped = set(redispatch_candidates(repo, mine, live_runs(mine, agents), capped_only=True)[2].values())
    except Problem:         # not in a repository: nothing to mark
        capped = set()
    shown = []
    for record in records:
        ended = parse_iso(record.get("ended_at"))
        if args.all or not record.get("ended_at") or (ended is not None and ended >= cutoff):
            row = dict(record, state=run_state(record, agents))
            if record.get("id") in capped:
                row["capped"] = True
            shown.append(row)
    shown.sort(key=lambda r: str(r.get("started_at")))
    if args.json:
        emit(wants_json(args), shown, "")
    elif not shown:
        print("No runs." if args.all else "No runs alive or ended in the last 24 h (--all lists every run).")
    else:
        rows = [("RUN", "TICKET", "VENUE", "STATE", "STARTED")]
        for r in shown:
            rows.append((str(r.get("id")), f"{os.path.basename(str(r.get('repo') or ''))} #{r.get('ticket')}",
                         str(r.get("venue")), r["state"] + (" capped" if r.get("capped") else ""),
                         str(r.get("started_at"))))
        print(table(rows))


def count(groups, key, item, kind):
    """Add one call of `kind` to the row of `groups` under `key`, made from `item` on its first call."""
    row = groups.setdefault(key, dict(item, calls=0, graphql=0, rest=0, refused=0))
    row["calls"] += 1
    if kind in ("graphql", "rest"):
        row[kind] += 1
    return row


def ranked(groups, keys):
    """The rows of `groups` by calls descending, then by group key, each with only `keys`."""
    return [{k: row[k] for k in keys} for _, row in sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1]["calls"], kv[0]))]


def cmd_budget_calls(args):
    """The gh call log of the last --hours hours (ghlimit.read_calls): totals, by tool, command, ticket and hour,
    and the busiest minute. Reads the log only; no gh call."""
    try:
        hours = float(args.hours)
    except ValueError:
        hours = float("nan")
    until = now().replace(microsecond=0)
    try:
        if not 0 < hours < float("inf"):
            raise OverflowError
        since = until - dt.timedelta(hours=hours)
    except OverflowError:
        raise Problem(f"--hours must be a number more than 0, not {args.hours!r}") from None
    lines = ghlimit.read_calls(since)
    totals = {"graphql": 0, "rest": 0, "refused": 0, "failed": 0}
    waited_ms = 0
    tools, commands, tickets, by_hour, minutes = {}, {}, {}, {}, {}
    for line in lines:
        at = parse_iso(line["at"]).astimezone(dt.timezone.utc)
        kind = line.get("kind")
        refused = line.get("refused") is True
        if kind in ("graphql", "rest"):
            totals[kind] += 1
        totals["refused"] += refused
        totals["failed"] += line.get("exit") != 0 and not refused
        waited = line.get("waited_ms")
        if isinstance(waited, (int, float)) and not isinstance(waited, bool) and abs(waited) < float("inf"):
            waited_ms += waited
        tool = str(line.get("tool") or "")
        count(tools, tool, {"tool": tool}, kind)["refused"] += refused
        cmd = str(line.get("cmd") or "")
        count(commands, (cmd, str(kind)), {"cmd": cmd, "kind": kind}, kind)
        ticket = line.get("ticket")
        if isinstance(ticket, int) and not isinstance(ticket, bool):
            repo = str(line.get("repo") or "")
            count(tickets, (repo, ticket), {"repo": repo, "ticket": ticket}, kind)
        hour = at.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:00:00Z")
        count(by_hour, hour, {"hour": hour}, kind)
        minute = at.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:00Z")
        minutes[minute] = minutes.get(minute, 0) + 1
    peak = min(minutes.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0])) if minutes else None
    data = {"since": iso(since), "until": iso(until), "hours": hours, "total": len(lines),
            "graphql": totals["graphql"], "rest": totals["rest"], "refused": totals["refused"],
            "failed": totals["failed"], "waited_seconds": waited_ms / 1000,
            "peak_minute": {"minute": peak[0], "calls": peak[1]} if peak else None,
            "by_tool": ranked(tools, ("tool", "calls", "graphql", "rest", "refused")),
            "by_command": ranked(commands, ("cmd", "kind", "calls")),
            "by_ticket": ranked(tickets, ("repo", "ticket", "calls", "graphql")),
            "by_hour": [{k: row[k] for k in ("hour", "calls", "graphql", "rest")}
                        for _, row in sorted(by_hour.items())]}
    if wants_json(args):
        emit(True, data, "")
        return
    window = str(int(hours)) if hours.is_integer() else repr(hours)   # 24, 0.5, 1234567: never 1.23457e+06
    if not lines:
        print(f"No gh calls logged in the last {window} h.")
        return
    parts = [f"gh calls in the last {window} h: {data['total']} (graphql {data['graphql']}, rest {data['rest']}), "
             f"{data['refused']} refused, {data['failed']} failed, {int(data['waited_seconds'])} s waiting; "
             f"peak {peak[1]} in one minute ({peak[0][:16]}Z)",
             table([("TOOL", "CALLS", "GRAPHQL", "REST", "REFUSED")]
                   + [(r["tool"], str(r["calls"]), str(r["graphql"]), str(r["rest"]), str(r["refused"]))
                      for r in data["by_tool"]]),
             table([("COMMAND", "KIND", "CALLS")]
                   + [(r["cmd"], str(r["kind"]), str(r["calls"])) for r in data["by_command"][:CALLS_TOP]])]
    if data["by_ticket"]:
        parts.append(table([("TICKET", "CALLS", "GRAPHQL")]
                           + [(f"{r['repo']} #{r['ticket']}", str(r["calls"]), str(r["graphql"]))
                              for r in data["by_ticket"]]))
    print("\n\n".join(parts))


def cmd_budget(args):
    if args.action == "calls":
        cmd_budget_calls(args)
        return
    budgets = load_budgets()
    action = args.action or "status"
    if action == "exhaust":
        if not args.hours > 0:
            raise Problem("--hours must be more than 0")
        if not args.reason.strip():
            raise Problem("--reason is empty")
        exhaust(budgets, args.name, args.reason, args.hours)
        names = [args.name]
    elif action == "reset":
        budgets[args.name] = {"exhausted_until": None, "reason": ""}
        write_json(budgets_path(), budgets)
        names = [args.name]
    else:
        names = list(BUDGETS) + sorted(k for k in budgets if k not in BUDGETS and isinstance(budgets[k], dict))
    data = {name: {"exhausted_until": budgets[name].get("exhausted_until"),
                   "reason": budgets[name].get("reason") or "",
                   "exhausted": exhausted_until(budgets[name]) is not None} for name in names}
    emit(wants_json(args), data, "\n".join(budget_line(name, budgets[name]) for name in names))


def cmd_worktrees(repo, args):
    if args.stale < 0:
        raise Problem("--stale must be 0 or more days")
    base = os.path.realpath(repo.worktrees_dir) + os.sep
    rows, gh_failed = [], None
    current = now()
    for entry in worktree_entries(repo.main, git_ok):
        path = os.path.realpath(entry.path)
        if not path.startswith(base) or entry.bare:
            continue
        when = None
        if os.path.isdir(path):
            log = git(path, "log", "-1", "--format=%ct")
            if log.returncode == 0 and log.stdout.strip().isdigit():
                when = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(int(log.stdout.strip()), dt.timezone.utc)
            status = git(path, "status", "--porcelain")
            dirty = status.returncode == 0 and bool(status.stdout.strip())
        else:
            dirty = False
        pr = None
        branch = entry.branch
        if branch and gh_failed is None:
            try:
                found = gh_json(repo, ["pr", "list", "--head", branch, "--state", "all", "--json",
                                       "number,state,isDraft", "--limit", "1"])
                if isinstance(found, list) and found and isinstance(found[0], dict):
                    pr = {"number": found[0].get("number"), "state": str(found[0].get("state") or "").upper(),
                          "draft": bool(found[0].get("isDraft"))}
            except Problem as err:
                gh_failed = err
                warn(f"PR states unknown: {err}")
        age_days = (current - when).total_seconds() / 86400 if when else None
        stale = age_days is not None and age_days > args.stale and not (pr and pr["state"] == "OPEN")
        rows.append({"path": path, "branch": branch, "last_commit": iso(when) if when else None,
                     "age_days": round(age_days, 2) if age_days is not None else None, "pr": pr,
                     "dirty": dirty, "missing": not os.path.isdir(path), "stale": stale})
    if args.json:
        emit(wants_json(args), rows, "")
        return
    if not rows:
        print("No ticket worktrees.")
        return
    lines = [("BRANCH", "AGE", "PR", "FLAGS", "PATH")]
    for r in rows:
        age = age_text(r["age_days"] * 86400) if r["age_days"] is not None else "?"
        pr = "-" if not r["pr"] else f"#{r['pr']['number']} {r['pr']['state'].lower()}" + \
            (" draft" if r["pr"]["draft"] else "")
        flags = ",".join(f for f in ("stale", "dirty", "missing") if r[f]) or "-"
        lines.append((r["branch"] or "(detached)", age, pr, flags, os.path.relpath(r["path"], repo.main)))
    print(table(lines))


# --------------------------------------------------------------- origin's ticket branches (#416)
TICKET_BRANCH_RE = re.compile(r"t/([0-9]+)-[^/]+")      # t/N-<slug>, the form start creates


def branch_ticket(branch):
    """N of a ticket branch t/N-<slug>, else None."""
    found = TICKET_BRANCH_RE.fullmatch(branch or "")
    return int(found.group(1)) if found and int(found.group(1)) > 0 else None


def origin_refs(repo, *patterns):
    """{ref: sha} of origin's refs matching `patterns`, read from origin now (`git ls-remote`), never from the local
    refs/remotes/origin/*, which lack what a cloud session or a CI fix pushed since the last fetch. Problem when
    origin cannot be read."""
    refs = {}
    for line in git_ok(repo.main, "ls-remote", "origin", *patterns).splitlines():
        sha, _, ref = line.partition("\t")
        if ref.strip():
            refs[ref.strip()] = sha.strip()
    return refs


def live_run_branches(repo):
    """{branch: run id} of this repository's live runs, by run_live (every venue)."""
    agents = Agents()
    return {r["branch"]: r.get("id") for r in load_runs()
            if of_repo(r, repo) and isinstance(r.get("branch"), str) and r["branch"] and run_live(r, agents)}


def judge_branch(repo, branch, tip, refs, live):
    """Origin's ticket branch `branch` at `tip`: {branch, ticket, tip, issue {state, state_reason} or None, pr (the
    newest, {number, state}) or None, stale, reason}. Stale only when its issue is CLOSED, none of its PRs is OPEN, no
    live run names it (`live`, live_run_branches) and `tip` is the head of one of its PRs (refs/pull/N/head in
    `refs`, read from origin) or, with no PR, its issue was closed as completed: the commits stay reachable or have
    landed. A failed or unreadable gh answer keeps it and is one of its reasons, never read as an answer. `reason`
    says why it is stale, or every reason it is kept."""
    n = branch_ticket(branch)
    kept, issue, prs = [], None, None
    if branch in live:
        kept.append(f"a live run names it ({live[branch]})")
    try:
        found = ticket_issue(repo, n)
        if not isinstance(found, dict) or not found.get("state"):
            raise Problem(f"gh issue view {n} printed no issue state")
        issue = {"state": str(found["state"]).upper(), "state_reason": str(found.get("stateReason") or "").upper()
                 or None}
    except Problem as err:
        kept.append(f"cannot read issue #{n}: {err}")
    try:
        prs = branch_prs(repo, branch, strict=True)
    except Problem as err:
        kept.append(f"cannot list its PRs: {err}")
    if issue is not None and issue["state"] != "CLOSED":
        kept.append(f"issue #{n} is {issue['state'].lower()}")
    held = None
    if prs:
        opened = [pr for pr in prs if str(pr.get("state", "")).upper() == "OPEN"]
        held = next((pr for pr in prs if refs.get(f"refs/pull/{pr.get('number')}/head") == tip), None)
        if opened:
            kept.append(f"PR #{opened[0].get('number')} is open")
        elif held is None:
            numbers = ", ".join(f"#{pr.get('number')}" for pr in prs)
            kept.append(f"its tip {tip[:7]} is the head of none of its PRs ({numbers}), so its later commits would "
                        f"be lost")
    elif prs == [] and issue is not None and issue["state"] == "CLOSED" and issue["state_reason"] != "COMPLETED":
        how = (issue["state_reason"] or "no reason").lower().replace("_", " ")
        kept.append(f"no PR holds its commits and #{n} was closed as {how}, not as completed")
    if kept:
        reason = "; ".join(kept)
    elif held is not None:
        reason = f"#{n} closed, PR #{held.get('number')} holds its tip"
    else:
        reason = f"#{n} closed as completed, no PR"
    newest = prs[0] if prs else None
    return {"branch": branch, "ticket": n, "tip": tip, "issue": issue,
            "pr": {"number": newest.get("number"), "state": str(newest.get("state") or "").upper()} if newest else None,
            "stale": not kept, "reason": reason}


def delete_origin_branch(repo, branch):
    """Delete origin's `branch` through the GitHub API, in the main checkout (whose repository `{owner}/{repo}`
    names, as for the tool's other gh calls); never through git push, so the pre-push hook and branch_guard go on
    refusing a raw delete. Problem with gh's error."""
    gh_json(repo, ["api", f"repos/{{owner}}/{{repo}}/git/refs/heads/{quote(branch)}", "-X", "DELETE"])


def cmd_branches(repo, args):
    trees = {e.branch for e in worktree_entries(repo.main, git_ok) if e.branch and os.path.isdir(e.path)}
    refs = origin_refs(repo, "refs/heads/t/*", "refs/pull/*/head")
    found = [(ref[len("refs/heads/"):], tip) for ref, tip in refs.items() if ref.startswith("refs/heads/")]
    branches = sorted(((branch_ticket(branch), branch, tip) for branch, tip in found
                       if branch_ticket(branch) is not None and branch not in trees))
    branches = [(branch, tip) for _, branch, tip in branches]
    live = live_run_branches(repo) if branches else {}
    rows = [judge_branch(repo, branch, tip, refs, live) for branch, tip in branches]
    if not args.prune:
        if wants_json(args):
            emit(True, rows, "")
        elif not rows:
            print("No ticket branches on origin without a worktree.")
        else:
            lines = [("BRANCH", "ISSUE", "PR", "VERDICT")]
            for r in rows:
                state = f"#{r['ticket']} {r['issue']['state'].lower()}" if r["issue"] else f"#{r['ticket']} ?"
                pr = f"#{r['pr']['number']} {r['pr']['state'].lower()}" if r["pr"] else "-"
                lines.append((r["branch"], state, pr, ("stale: " if r["stale"] else "keep: ") + r["reason"]))
            print(table(lines))
        return
    failed = 0
    for r in rows:
        r["deleted"] = False
        if not r["stale"]:
            line = f"kept origin/{r['branch']}: {r['reason']}"
        else:
            try:
                delete_origin_branch(repo, r["branch"])
                r["deleted"] = True
                line = f"deleted origin/{r['branch']}: {r['reason']}"
            except Problem as err:
                failed += 1
                r["error"] = str(err)
                line = f"not deleted origin/{r['branch']}: {err}"
        if not wants_json(args):
            print(one_line(line), flush=True)
    if wants_json(args):
        emit(True, rows, "")
    if failed:
        raise Problem(f"{failed} of {sum(1 for r in rows if r['stale'])} stale branches could not be deleted")


def prune_after_remove(repo, branch):
    """worktree remove's remote step, by judge_branch as `branches --prune`: origin's ticket branch deleted when stale
    (`deleted origin/<branch>: <why>` on stdout), else kept with its reasons (one warning); nothing for a branch that
    is no ticket branch or that origin does not have. A failed DELETE is Problem."""
    if branch_ticket(branch) is None:
        return
    try:
        refs = origin_refs(repo, f"refs/heads/{branch}", "refs/pull/*/head")
    except Problem as err:
        warn(f"kept origin/{branch}: cannot read origin: {err}")
        return
    tip = refs.get(f"refs/heads/{branch}")
    if tip is None:
        return
    row = judge_branch(repo, branch, tip, refs, live_run_branches(repo))
    if not row["stale"]:
        warn(f"kept origin/{branch}: {row['reason']}")
        return
    try:
        delete_origin_branch(repo, branch)
    except Problem as err:
        raise Problem(f"origin/{branch} not deleted: {err}") from None
    print(one_line(f"deleted origin/{branch}: {row['reason']}"), flush=True)


# --------------------------------------------------------------- backups
def backup_main(args):
    """The main checkout backup acts for: --repo (which must be in a repository), else CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, else the
    cwd's; None outside a repository."""
    try:
        return repo_facts(args.repo or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR") or os.getcwd(), git, last_line)[2]
    except NotARepository as exc:
        if args.repo:
            raise Problem(str(exc)) from None
        return None
    except RepoError as exc:
        raise Problem(str(exc)) from None


def size_text(count):
    """Bytes in decimal units, as Finder shows them: 512 B, 3.4 kB, 1.2 MB."""
    if count < 1000:
        return f"{count} B"
    for unit in ("kB", "MB", "GB", "TB"):
        count /= 1000
        if count < 999.95 or unit == "TB":
            return f"{count:.1f} {unit}"


def cmd_backup_list(main, args):
    found = backups.snapshots(main, everything=args.all or main is None)
    if args.json:
        emit(True, found, "")
        return
    if not found:
        print("No backups.")
        return
    current, rows = time.time(), [("ID", "AGE", "ITEMS", "SIZE", "COMMAND")]
    for manifest in found:
        then = parse_iso_seconds(manifest.get("at"))
        items = [i for i in manifest["items"] if isinstance(i, dict)]
        refs = [r for r in manifest.get("refs") or [] if isinstance(r, dict)]
        size = sum(i["bytes"] for i in items if isinstance(i.get("bytes"), int) and not isinstance(i["bytes"], bool))
        rows.append((manifest["id"], ago_text(then, current) if then is not None else "?", str(len(items) + len(refs)),
                     size_text(size), one_line(manifest.get("command") or "")))
    print(table(rows))


def cmd_backup_restore(main, args):
    def progress(kind, value):
        if args.json:
            return
        if kind == "saved":
            count = len(value["items"])
            print(f"backup {value['id']} holds the {count} path{'' if count == 1 else 's'} this restore replaces",
                  flush=True)
        elif kind == "ref":
            print(value, flush=True)
        else:
            print(f"restored {value}", flush=True)

    result = backups.restore(main, args.id, only=args.path, to=args.to, force=args.force, cwd=os.getcwd(),
                             command=" ".join(["harness-work"] + [shlex.quote(a) for a in sys.argv[1:]]),
                             progress=progress)
    if args.json:
        emit(True, result, "")


def cmd_backup(args):
    main = backup_main(args)
    try:
        (cmd_backup_list if args.action == "list" else cmd_backup_restore)(main, args)
    except backups.BackupError as err:
        raise Problem(str(err)) from None


def cmd_worktree_remove(repo, args):
    branch = args.branch[len("refs/heads/"):] if args.branch.startswith("refs/heads/") else args.branch
    if branch in ("main", "master"):
        raise Problem(f"refusing to remove {branch}")
    git(repo.main, "worktree", "prune")
    entry = next((e for e in worktree_entries(repo.main, git_ok) if e.branch == branch), None)
    has_branch = ref_exists(repo, f"refs/heads/{branch}")
    if entry is None and not has_branch:
        raise Problem(f"no worktree and no local branch {branch}")
    done = []
    if entry is not None:
        path = os.path.realpath(entry.path)
        if path == repo.main:
            raise Problem(f"{branch} is checked out in the main checkout {repo.main}; switch it to main first")
        status = git_ok(path, "status", "--porcelain")
        changed = [line[3:] for line in status.splitlines() if line.strip()]
        if changed and not args.discard:
            more = f" and {len(changed) - DIRTY_SHOWN} more" if len(changed) > DIRTY_SHOWN else ""
            raise Problem(f"{path} has uncommitted changes: {', '.join(changed[:DIRTY_SHOWN])}{more}; "
                          "commit and push them, or pass --discard to throw them away")
        git_ok(repo.main, "worktree", "remove", *(["--force"] if args.discard else []), path)
        done.append(f"removed worktree {path}")
    if has_branch:
        git_ok(repo.main, "branch", "-D", branch)
        done.append(f"deleted branch {branch}")
    print("\n".join(done), flush=True)
    prune_after_remove(repo, branch)


# --------------------------------------------------------------- launchd (#164; harness-digest's are the model)
def plist_path():
    return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "Library", "LaunchAgents", f"{LAUNCHD_LABEL}.plist")


def launchctl(args):
    """(exit code, first line of output) of a launchctl call (HARNESS_LAUNCHCTL when set); never raises."""
    exe = os.environ.get("HARNESS_LAUNCHCTL") or "launchctl"
    try:
        done = subprocess.run([exe] + args, capture_output=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace", timeout=30,
                              stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as err:
        return 1, str(getattr(err, "strerror", None) or err)
    return done.returncode, first_line(done.stderr) or first_line(done.stdout) or f"exit {done.returncode}"


def install_launchd():
    """Write the LaunchAgent that runs `dispatch --all-projects --max 8` at minute 0 of every hour and load it.
    StartCalendarInterval, not StartInterval: launchd runs a calendar job missed while the Mac slept once on wake."""
    path = plist_path()
    script = os.path.realpath(os.path.abspath(__file__))
    job_path = ":".join(["/opt/homebrew/bin", "/usr/local/bin", os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".local", "bin"),
                         "/usr/bin", "/bin"])
    python = shutil.which("python3", path=job_path) or sys.executable    # the python3 the job's own PATH finds
    log = harness_home("dispatch", "launchd.log")
    job = {"Label": LAUNCHD_LABEL,
           "ProgramArguments": [python, script, "dispatch", "--all-projects", "--max", str(ALL_PROJECTS_MAX)],
           "StartCalendarInterval": {"Minute": 0}, "EnvironmentVariables": {"PATH": job_path},
           "StandardOutPath": log, "StandardErrorPath": log, "RunAtLoad": False}
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(log), exist_ok=True)
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        with open(path, "wb") as fh:
            plistlib.dump(job, fh)
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"cannot write {path}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    domain = f"gui/{os.getuid()}"
    launchctl(["bootout", f"{domain}/{LAUNCHD_LABEL}"])      # an older copy; failing means none was loaded
    code, why = launchctl(["bootstrap", domain, path])
    if code == 0:
        print(f"harness-work: wrote {path} and loaded it (launchctl bootstrap {domain}); it dispatches every "
              f"opted-in project hourly at minute 0, log {log}")
        return
    code2, why2 = launchctl(["load", "-w", path])
    if code2 == 0:
        print(f"harness-work: wrote {path}; launchctl bootstrap failed ({why}), loaded it with launchctl load -w "
              f"instead; it dispatches every opted-in project hourly at minute 0, log {log}")
        return
    raise Problem(f"wrote {path} but could not load it: launchctl bootstrap: {why}; launchctl load -w: {why2}")


def uninstall_launchd():
    path = plist_path()
    code, why = launchctl(["bootout", f"gui/{os.getuid()}/{LAUNCHD_LABEL}"])
    unloaded = "unloaded it (launchctl bootout)" if code == 0 else f"it was not loaded ({why})"
    try:
        os.remove(path)
        removed = f"removed {path}"
    except FileNotFoundError:
        removed = f"no {path} to remove"
    except OSError as err:
        raise Problem(f"{unloaded}; cannot remove {path}: {err.strerror or err}") from None
    print(f"harness-work: {unloaded}; {removed}")


# --------------------------------------------------------------- arguments
def ticket_list(text):
    """An argparse `type=`: issue numbers separated by commas, in the order given, once each."""
    out = []
    for part in text.split(","):
        n = issue_number(part.strip())
        if n not in out:
            out.append(n)
    return out


def parser():
    repo_help = "the project (default: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, else the cwd's repository)"
    with_repo = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    with_repo.add_argument("--repo", metavar="PATH", help=repo_help)
    with_json = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    with_json.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print JSON")
    nested_json = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)     # never resets a --json given before the action
    nested_json.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", default=argparse.SUPPRESS, help="print JSON")
    ap = Parser(prog="harness-work", description="Ticket worktrees, attempts, dispatch, runs and budgets.")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd",
                            metavar="{start,attempt,stage,cost,dispatch,cloud,runs,waves,wave,budget,worktrees,"
                                    "branches,worktree,backup}")
    sub.required = True

    start = sub.add_parser("start", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                           help="branch and worktree for a ticket, status in-progress, its context and answers")
    start.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")
    start.add_argument("--venue", default="interactive", choices=("interactive",) + VENUES + ("cloud",),
                       help="named in the start comment (dispatch passes its own)")

    attempt = sub.add_parser("attempt", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                             help="record a stage's result; prints done, retry, escalate <tier> [<effort>] or "
                                  "park (escalate opus, then escalate opus xhigh, then park; fix retries, then "
                                  "park; a breaker failure is done)")
    attempt.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")
    attempt.add_argument("stage", choices=STAGES)
    attempt.add_argument("result", choices=("pass", "fail"))
    attempt.add_argument("--tier", choices=TIERS, help="the tier this attempt ran at (default: the stage's route)")
    attempt.add_argument("--effort", choices=EFFORTS,
                         help="the effort this attempt ran at (default: the stage route's effort when it ran at that "
                              "route's tier, else none)")

    stage = sub.add_parser("stage", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                           help="record a stage's result as attempt does, then print the work loop's next step")
    stage.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")
    stage.add_argument("stage", choices=STAGES)
    stage.add_argument("result", choices=("pass", "fail"))
    stage.add_argument("--tier", choices=TIERS, help="the tier this attempt ran at (default: the stage's route)")
    stage.add_argument("--effort", choices=EFFORTS,
                       help="the effort this attempt ran at (default: the stage route's effort when it ran at that "
                            "route's tier, else none)")

    cost_ = sub.add_parser("cost", parents=[with_repo],
                           help="a ticket's tokens and model time per stage and model, with its rounds; "
                                "saves cost/<N>.json")
    cost_.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")
    cost_.add_argument("--pr", type=issue_number, metavar="P", help="the pull request, kept in the record")
    output = cost_.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    output.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print the record")
    output.add_argument("--markdown", action="store_true", help="print the Cost block of the Resolution")

    dispatch = sub.add_parser("dispatch", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                              help="start and launch a session per ready ticket")
    dispatch.add_argument("--max", type=int, default=None,
                          help=f"live runs at most (default {DISPATCH_MAX}; with --all-projects {ALL_PROJECTS_MAX}, "
                               f"counted across every project)")
    dispatch.add_argument("--venue", choices=VENUES,
                          help="default: bg (the subscription; held while the subscription budget is exhausted); "
                               "headless bills the API key and is refused while the api budget is exhausted")
    dispatch.add_argument("--api", action="store_true",
                          help="alias for --venue headless: runs headless, billed to the API key")
    dispatch.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the plan; start and launch nothing")
    dispatch.add_argument("--all-projects", action="store_true",
                          help=f"every registered project whose .claude/settings.json at origin/main sets "
                               f"{AUTODISPATCH} to 1 and that has no open incident issue, in bg; not with --api, "
                               f"--venue headless, --only, --after or --repo")
    job = dispatch.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    job.add_argument("--install-launchd", action="store_true",
                     help=f"run dispatch --all-projects --max {ALL_PROJECTS_MAX} hourly (a LaunchAgent); "
                          f"dispatches nothing now")
    job.add_argument("--uninstall-launchd", action="store_true", help="remove that LaunchAgent")
    pick = dispatch.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    pick.add_argument("--only", type=ticket_list, metavar="N[,N...]",
                      help="consider only these tickets (each ready, or in progress with an ended run); "
                           "any other is skipped with the reason")
    pick.add_argument("--after", type=issue_number, metavar="N",
                      help="consider the ready tickets ticket N blocked, else the first ready ticket without a "
                           "live run")

    cloud = sub.add_parser("cloud", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                           help="start a ticket, push its branch and launch a Claude cloud session on it")
    cloud.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")

    runs = sub.add_parser("runs", parents=[with_json], help="dispatched runs, alive or ended in the last 24 h")
    runs.add_argument("--sweep", action="store_true", help="close ended runs and classify their outcome")
    runs.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="every run on record")

    waves_ = sub.add_parser("waves", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                            help="this repository's waves (the tickets one dispatch launched) and where each stands")
    waves_.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="every wave, those whose tickets are all closed too")
    waves_.add_argument("--refresh", action="store_true",
                        help="ask gh for each waiting ticket's status instead of trusting its cache")

    wave = sub.add_parser("wave", help="one wave")
    wave_sub = wave.add_subparsers(dest="action", metavar="{drop}")
    wave_sub.required = True
    drop = wave_sub.add_parser("drop", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                               help="take a ticket out of a wave whose review was not launched")
    drop.add_argument("id", metavar="ID")
    drop.add_argument("number", type=issue_number, metavar="N")

    budget = sub.add_parser("budget", parents=[with_json], help="the api, cloud and subscription budgets")
    budget_sub = budget.add_subparsers(dest="action", metavar="{status,exhaust,reset,calls}")
    budget_sub.add_parser("status", parents=[nested_json], help="each budget's state (the default)")
    ex = budget_sub.add_parser("exhaust", parents=[nested_json], help="mark a budget exhausted")
    ex.add_argument("name", choices=BUDGETS)
    ex.add_argument("--reason", required=True, metavar="TEXT")
    ex.add_argument("--hours", type=float, default=EXHAUST_HOURS, help="default 24")
    reset = budget_sub.add_parser("reset", parents=[nested_json], help="mark a budget available")
    reset.add_argument("name", choices=BUDGETS)
    calls = budget_sub.add_parser("calls", parents=[nested_json],
                                  help="the gh call log: totals by tool, command, ticket and hour, the busiest minute")
    calls.add_argument("--hours", default=str(CALLS_HOURS), metavar="H",
                       help="the window, default 24 (checked by the command: a bad value is one line, exit 1)")

    wts = sub.add_parser("worktrees", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                         help="the ticket worktrees with age, PR state and the stale flag")
    wts.add_argument("--stale", type=float, default=7, metavar="DAYS", help="default 7")

    brs = sub.add_parser("branches", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                         help="origin's t/* branches without a worktree, with issue, newest PR and the stale flag")
    brs.add_argument("--prune", action="store_true",
                     help="delete each stale branch through the GitHub API; print deleted or kept with the reason")

    wt = sub.add_parser("worktree", help="one ticket worktree")
    wt_sub = wt.add_subparsers(dest="action", metavar="{remove}")
    wt_sub.required = True
    rm = wt_sub.add_parser("remove", parents=[with_repo],
                           help="remove a worktree and delete its branch, and origin's when it is stale")
    rm.add_argument("branch")
    rm.add_argument("--discard", action="store_true", help="remove it even with uncommitted changes")

    backup = sub.add_parser("backup", help="the snapshots taken before destructive commands, and their restore")
    backup_sub = backup.add_subparsers(dest="action", metavar="{list,restore}")
    backup_sub.required = True
    blist = backup_sub.add_parser("list", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                                  help="this repository's snapshots, newest first")
    blist.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="every snapshot in ~/.claude/harness/backups/ too")
    brestore = backup_sub.add_parser("restore", parents=[with_repo, with_json],
                                     help="put a snapshot's items back; refused over an existing path without --force")
    brestore.add_argument("id", metavar="ID")
    brestore.add_argument("--path", metavar="P", help="only the items at or under P")
    brestore.add_argument("--to", metavar="DIR", help="under DIR instead of at the original paths")
    brestore.add_argument("--force", action="store_true",
                          help="snapshot the existing paths it replaces first, then replace them")
    return ap


def main():
    ap = parser()
    args = ap.parse_args()
    if args.cmd == "dispatch":
        given = [flag for flag, on in (("--all-projects", args.all_projects), ("--max", args.max is not None),
                                       ("--venue", args.venue), ("--api", args.api), ("--dry-run", args.dry_run),
                                       ("--only", args.only is not None), ("--after", args.after is not None),
                                       ("--repo", args.repo)) if on]
        if (args.install_launchd or args.uninstall_launchd) and given:
            ap.error(f"dispatch: --install-launchd and --uninstall-launchd take no {given[0]}")
        if args.api:
            if args.venue == "bg":
                ap.error("dispatch: --api is --venue headless and cannot go with --venue bg")
            args.venue = "headless"
        if args.all_projects:
            if args.venue == "headless":
                ap.error("dispatch: --all-projects launches bg sessions on the subscription and cannot go with "
                         + ("--api" if args.api else "--venue headless"))
            other = next((flag for flag in ("--only", "--after", "--repo") if flag in given), None)
            if other:
                ap.error(f"dispatch: --all-projects cannot go with {other}")
        if args.max is None:
            args.max = ALL_PROJECTS_MAX if args.all_projects else DISPATCH_MAX
    try:
        now()  # an unreadable HARNESS_NOW stops here, before any command has written anything
        if args.cmd == "runs":
            cmd_runs(args)
        elif args.cmd == "budget":
            cmd_budget(args)
        elif args.cmd == "backup":
            cmd_backup(args)
        elif args.cmd == "dispatch" and args.install_launchd:
            install_launchd()
        elif args.cmd == "dispatch" and args.uninstall_launchd:
            uninstall_launchd()
        elif args.cmd == "dispatch" and args.all_projects:
            cmd_dispatch_all(args)
        else:
            command = {"start": cmd_start, "attempt": cmd_attempt, "stage": cmd_stage, "cost": cmd_cost, "dispatch": cmd_dispatch,
                       "cloud": cmd_cloud, "waves": cmd_waves, "wave": cmd_wave_drop, "worktrees": cmd_worktrees,
                       "branches": cmd_branches, "worktree": cmd_worktree_remove}[args.cmd]
            command(open_repo(args.repo), args)
    except Problem as err:
        sys.exit(f"harness-work: {one_line(err)}")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    run_main("harness-work", main)
